[Term]
id: BFO:0000001
name: entity
def: "An entity is anything that exists or has existed or will exist." []
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q35120
property_value: Property:P5191 "entitātem" xsd:string
property_value: schema:alternateName "entities" xsd:string

[Term]
id: BFO:0000002
name: continuant
def: "A continuant is an entity that persists, endures, or continues to exist through time while maintaining its identity." []
def: "An entity that exists in full at any time in which it exists at all, persists through time while maintaining its identity and has no temporal parts." []
is_a: BFO:0000001 ! entity
property_value: Property:P5191 "continuant" xsd:string
property_value: Property:P5191 "continuānt" xsd:string
property_value: schema:alternateName "continuants" xsd:string

[Term]
id: BFO:0000003
name: occurrent
def: "An occurrent is an entity that unfolds itself in time or it is the instantaneous boundary of such an entity (for example a beginning or an ending) or it is a temporal or spatiotemporal region which such an entity occupies a temporal region or a spatiotemporal region." []
is_a: BFO:0000001 ! entity
property_value: Property:P5191 "occurrent" xsd:string
property_value: Property:P5191 "occurrēns" xsd:string
property_value: schema:alternateName "occurrents" xsd:string

[Term]
id: BFO:0000004
name: independent continuant
def: "b is an independent continuant = Def. b is a continuant which is such that there is no c and no t such that b s-depends_on c at t." []
is_a: BFO:0000002 ! continuant
property_value: Property:P5191 BFO:0000002
property_value: Property:P5191 "independent" xsd:string
property_value: schema:alternateName "independent continuants" xsd:string

[Term]
id: BFO:0000008
name: temporal region
def: "A region of time." []
is_a: BFO:0000003 ! occurrent
property_value: Property:P1402 "http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma312872" xsd:string
property_value: schema:alternateName "temporal regions" xsd:string

[Term]
id: BFO:0000015
name: process
def: "A process is an entity that is identifiable only through the unfolding of time, has temporal parts, and unless otherwise specified/predicted, cannot be identified from any instant of time in which it exists." []
synonym: "processed" RELATED []
synonym: "processing" RELATED []
synonym: "processual" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Process
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3249551
is_a: BFO:0000003 ! occurrent
property_value: Property:P5191 "procès" xsd:string
property_value: Property:P5191 "procés" xsd:string
property_value: Property:P5191 "prōcessus" xsd:string
property_value: schema:alternateName "processes" xsd:string

[Term]
id: BFO:0000017
name: realizable entity
def: "A realizable entity is an attribute that is exhibited under some condition and is realized in some process." []
is_a: BFO:0000020 ! specifically dependent continuant
is_a: SIO:000614 ! attribute
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "realisable entity" xsd:string {schema:alternateName="realisable entities"}
property_value: Property:P5191 BFO:0000001
property_value: Property:P5191 "realizable" xsd:string
property_value: schema:alternateName "realizable entities" xsd:string

[Term]
id: BFO:0000019
name: quality
def: "A dependent entity that inheres in a bearer by virtue of how the bearer is related to other entities." []
def: "A quality is a specifically dependent continuant that, in contrast to roles and dispositions, does not require any further process in order to be realized." []
def: "A quality is an attribute that is intrinsically associated with its bearer (or its parts), but whose presence/absence and observed/measured value may vary." []
comment: The etymology of "quality" is fairly well elucidated coming from Middle English, from Old French qualité, from Latin qualitatem, accusative of qualitas, from qualis (“of what kind”), from Proto-Indo-European *kʷo- (“who, how”). Cicero coined qualitas as a calque to translate the Ancient Greek word ποιότης (poiótēs, “quality”), coined by Plato from ποῖος (poîos, “of what nature, of what kind”).
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quality_(philosophy)
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1207505
is_a: BFO:0000020 ! specifically dependent continuant
is_a: SIO:000614 ! attribute
property_value: Property:P5191 "qualitatem" xsd:string
property_value: Property:P5191 "qualité" xsd:string
property_value: schema:alternateName "qualities" xsd:string

[Term]
id: BFO:0000020
name: specifically dependent continuant
def: "b is a specifically dependent continuant = Def. b is a continuant & there is some independent continuant c which is not a spatial region and which is such that b s-depends_on c at every time t during the course of b’s existence." []
is_a: BFO:0000002 ! continuant
property_value: Property:P5191 BFO:0000002
property_value: Property:P5191 "dependent" xsd:string
property_value: Property:P5191 "specifically" xsd:string
property_value: schema:alternateName "specifically dependent continuants" xsd:string

[Term]
id: BFO:0000023
name: role
def: "A realizable entity the manifestation of which brings about some result or end that is not essential to a continuant in virtue of the kind of thing that it is but that can be served or participated in by that kind of continuant in some kinds of natural, social or institutional contexts." []
def: "A role is a realizable entity that describes behaviours, rights and obligations of an entity in some particular circumstance." []
is_a: BFO:0000017 ! realizable entity
