[Term]
id: CHEBI:16236
name: ethanol
def: "A clear, colorless liquid rapidly absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract and distributed throughout the body. It has bactericidal activity and is used often as a topical disinfectant. It is widely used as a solvent and preservative in pharmaceutical preparations as well as serving as the primary ingredient in alcoholic beverages." []
def: "A primary alcohol that is ethane in which one of the hydrogens is substituted by a hydroxy group." []
