[Term]
id: CHEBI:58987
name: sildenafil citrate
def: "A phosphodiesterase type-5 inhibitor; vasodilator agent and urological agent that is used in the treatment of erectile dysfunction and primary pulmonary hypertension." []
def: "The citrate salt form of sildenafil, an orally bioavailable pyrazolopyrimidinone derivative structurally related to zaprinast, with vasodilating and potential anti-inflammatory activities. Upon oral administration, sildenafil selectively targets and inhibits cyclic guanosine monophosphate (cGMP)-specific phosphodiesterase type 5 (PDE5), thereby inhibiting the PDE5-mediated degradation of cGMP found in smooth muscle and increasing cGMP availability. This results in prolonged smooth muscle relaxation in the corpus cavernosum of the penis, thereby causing vasodilation, blood engorgement and a prolonged penile erection. In the smooth muscle of the pulmonary vasculature, the increase in cGMP results in smooth muscle relaxation, vasodilation of the pulmonary vascular bed, relieving pulmonary hypertension and increasing blood flow in the lungs. In addition, sildenafil may reduce airway inflammation and mucus production." []
def: "The citrate salt of sildenafil." []
is_a: CHEBI:50744 ! citrate salt
property_value: Property:P1748 "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C26670" xsd:anyURI
property_value: Property:P3345 "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/221161" xsd:anyURI
property_value: Property:P486 "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D000068677" xsd:anyURI
property_value: Property:P5806 "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/SNOMEDCT/108482004" xsd:anyURI
property_value: Property:P683 "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_58987" xsd:anyURI

