[Term]
id: DOID:12139
name: dysthymic disorder
def: "A mood disorder that involves the presence of a low mood almost daily over a span of at least two years." []
def: "Chronically depressed mood that occurs for most of the day more days than not for at least 2 years. The required minimum duration in children to make this diagnosis is 1 year. During periods of depressed mood, at least 2 of the following additional symptoms are present: poor appetite or overeating, insomnia or hypersomnia, low energy or fatigue, low self esteem, poor concentration or difficulty making decisions, and feelings of hopelessness." []
