[Term]
id: GAZ:00000556
name: East Africa
def: "A vast geographical and geological feature, approximately 6,000 km in length, which runs from northern Syria in Southwest Asia to central Mozambique in East Africa. Caused by the geological process of rifting, it is a complex feature where several plates of the earth's crust join. The rift valley varies in width from thirty to one hundred km, and in depth from a few hundred to several thousand meters." []
synonym: "Central and Eastern Africa" BROAD [] {terms:isReferencedBy="https://books.google.com/books?id=irYUAQAAIAAJ", hasSynonym="central and eastern Africa", hasSynonym="Africa, central & eastern"}
