[Term]
id: GAZ:00002472
name: South Asia
def: "The southern region of the Asian continent, which comprises the sub-Himalayan SAARC (South Asian Association for Regional Cooperation) countries and, for some authorities, adjoining countries to the west and east. Topographically, it is dominated by the Indian Plate, which rises above sea level as Nepal and northern parts of India situated south of the Himalayas and the Hindu Kush. South Asia is bounded on the south by the Indian Ocean and on land (clockwise, from west) by West Asia, Central Asia, East Asia, and Southeast Asia." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Asia
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q771405
