[Term]
id: GAZ:00003101
name: Italian Peninsula
def: "A peninsula extending from the southern Alps in the north to the central Mediterranean Sea in the south. It is nicknamed lo Stivale (the Boot). Three smaller peninsulas contribute to this characteristic shape, namely Calabria (the \"toe\"), Salento (the \"heel\") and Gargano (the \"spur\")." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italian_Peninsula
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q145694
is_a: GAZ:00000464 ! Europe

[Term]
id: GAZ:00003201
name: special administrative region of China
def: "Any of various areas in China designated as special administrative regions, that is a type of provincial-level administrative divisions of the People's Republic of China directly under Central People's Government. As a region, they possess the highest degree of autonomy in China. Despite the relative autonomy that the Central People's Government affords special administrative regions, the National People's Congress is still able to unilaterally write laws in secret for special administrative regions that are not read publicly until they are passed." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Special_administrative_regions_of_China
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special_administrative_regions_of_China
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q779415
