[Term]
id: GAZ:00003787
name: Kanto Region
def: "A region of Japan, in the middle east coast of Honshu Island. It encompasses seven prefectures which overlaps the Greater Tokyo Area: Gunma, Tochigi, Ibaraki, Saitama, Tokyo, Chiba, and Kanagawa. Within its boundaries, slightly more than 40 percent of the land area is the Kanto plain. The rest consists of the hills and mountains that form the land borders." []
