[Term]
id: GAZ:00003981
name: British Overseas Territory
def: "Any of various territories all with a constitutional and historical link with the United Kingdom. They are the last remnants of the former British Empire and do not form part of the United Kingdom itself. Some of the permanently inhabited territories are internally self-governing, with the UK retaining responsibility for defence and foreign relations with foreign and defence not extending to Norfolk Island. Three of the territories are inhabited only by a transitory population of military or scientific personnel." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Overseas_Territories
