[Term]
id: GO:0000746
name: genetic conjugation
def: "A parasexual process in bacteria; algae; fungi; and ciliate eukaryota for achieving exchange of chromosome material during fusion of two cells. In bacteria, this is a uni-directional transfer of genetic material; in protozoa it is a bi-directional exchange. In algae and fungi, it is a form of sexual reproduction, with the union of male and female gametes." []
def: "The union or introduction of genetic information from compatible mating types that results in a genetically different individual. Conjugation requires direct cellular contact between the organisms." []
synonym: "zygosis" NARROW [] {def="The union of gametes to form a zygote.", schema:alternateName="zygoses", terms:isReferencedBy="https://books.google.com/books/?id=ymkYAAAAIAAJ"}
is_a: GO:0044764 ! multi-organism cellular process
