[Term]
id: GSSO:000109
name: interseks
name: interseks {terms:isReferencedBy="https://web.archive.org/web/20190123175918/https://oramrefugee.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/Glossary-PDF.pdf"}
name: intersex
name: intersex {xref="https://lgbt.dk/ordbog/intersex/"}
name: intersexe {terms:isReferencedBy="https://web.archive.org/web/20190123175918/https://oramrefugee.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/Glossary-PDF.pdf"}
name: intersexo {terms:isReferencedBy="https://web.archive.org/web/20210121145426/https://nonbinary.wiki/wiki/Glossary_of_Brazilian_Portuguese_gender_and_sex_terminology"}
name: intersexualidad {terms:isReferencedBy="https://web.archive.org/web/20200102232435/lgbthealtheducation.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/National-LGBT-Health-Education-Center-Glossary.SPANISH-2018.pdf"}
name: ثنائي الجنس
name: मध्यलिंग
def: "Intersex is an umbrella term with a complex history. It is usually used to refer to persons with congenital conditions which involve differences in the many intertwined processes of sexual development." []
comment: It is important to note that some transgender persons are intersex, but not all, and vice versa. Terms like "ultergender" and "ipsogender" help clarify the ways these terms might overlap. While some studies have purported that small segments of the trans community might have traits that some consider intersex, the association of transgender with intersex in absolutes is often linked to transmedicalist ideologies. The Transgender Professional Association for Transgender Health (TPATH) notes in its guidelines: "While it may be appropriate to discuss intersections of intersex and trans experience, please do not erase the specificity of intersex experiences, for instance through conflating intersex with trans... In discussing these issues, we ask that endosexual transgender (i.e. not intersex) participants recognize their privilege in, for instance, not having faced the risk of infant genital mutilation or other non-consensual medical interventions during childhood."
synonym: "intersex state" RELATED []
synonym: "intersex status" RELATED []
