[Term]
id: GSSO:000113
name: chromosomal sex
def: "Sex as determined by the presence of particular sex chromosomes or combinations of sex chromosomes, without regard to phenotypic manifestations." []
comment: It is almost always preferable to include the specific karyotype (XX, XY, etc.) rather than "chromosomal male" or "chromosomal female". Additionally, avoid usage unless the patient's karyotype is actually known and confirmed via laboratory reports.
synonym: "GSSO:000104" BROAD []
synonym: "GSSO:000114" RELATED []
synonym: "karyotypic sex" RELATED []
is_a: GSSO:000104 ! genotypic sex
property_value: Property:P5191 GO:0005694
property_value: Property:P5191 NCIT:C28421
property_value: terms:isReferencedBy https://books.google.com/books/?id=ymkYAAAAIAAJ

[Term]
id: GSSO:000114
name: genetic sex
def: "Sex as determined by the presence and/or activation of particular genes or combinations of genes, without regard to phenotypic manifestations." []
synonym: "GSSO:000104" BROAD []
synonym: "GSSO:000113" RELATED []
is_a: GSSO:000104 ! genotypic sex
property_value: Property:P5191 NCIT:C28421

[Term]
id: GSSO:000115
name: sex-determination system
def: "A biological system that determines the development of sexual characteristics in an organism." []
synonym: "sex determination system" EXACT []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sex-determination_system
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q594595
is_a: GO:0007530 ! sex determination
property_value: schema:alternateName "sex-determination systems" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:000116
name: X0 sex-determination system
def: "A system that determines the sex of offspring among most arachnids, almost all apterygote and paleopteran insects, most exoptergote insects, and some nematodes, crustaceans, gastropod molluscs, and bony fish. In this system, there is only one sex chromosome, referred to as X. Males only have one X chromosome (X0), while females have two (XX)." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X0_sex-determination_system
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q607251
is_a: GSSO:000115 ! sex-determination system

[Term]
id: GSSO:000117
name: XY sex-determination system
def: "The sex-determination system found in humans, most other mammals, some insects (Drosophila), some snakes, and some plants (Ginkgo). In this system, the sex of an individual is determined by a pair of sex chromosomes. Females typically have two of the same kind of sex chromosome (XX), and are called the homogametic sex. Males typically have two different kinds of sex chromosomes (XY), and are called the heterogametic sex." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XY_sex-determination_system
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1604486
is_a: GSSO:000115 ! sex-determination system

[Term]
id: GSSO:000118
name: Z0 sex-determination system
def: "A system that determines the sex of offspring in several moths. In those species, males have two Z chromosomes whereas females have one." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Z0_sex-determination_system
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q8062889
is_a: GSSO:000115 ! sex-determination system

[Term]
id: GSSO:000119
name: ZW sex-determination system
def: "A chromosomal system that determines the sex of offspring in birds, some fish and crustaceans such as the giant river prawn, some insects (including butterflies and moths), and some reptiles, including Komodo dragons. In this system, female has a pair of dissimilar ZW chromosomes and male has two similar ZZ chromosomes." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ZW_sex-determination_system
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q135752
is_a: GSSO:000115 ! sex-determination system

[Term]
id: GSSO:000120
name: temperature-dependent sex determination
def: "A type of environmental sex determination in which the temperatures experienced during embryonic/larval development determine the sex of the offspring." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temperature-dependent_sex_determination
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1753424
is_a: GSSO:000107 ! environmental sex determination
property_value: Property:P1813 "TSD" xsd:string
property_value: wiki:Q1823134 "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2017003147" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: GSSO:000121
name: haplodiploid sex-determination system
def: "A sex-determination system in which males develop from unfertilized eggs and are haploid, and females develop from fertilized eggs and are diploid. Haplodiploidy determines the sex in all members of the insect orders Hymenoptera (bees, ants, and wasps) and Thysanoptera ('thrips'). The system also occurs sporadically in some spider mites, Hemiptera, Coleoptera (bark beetles), and rotifers." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haplodiploidy
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1098692
is_a: GSSO:000115 ! sex-determination system
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "arrhenotoky" xsd:string
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "haplodiploidy" xsd:string

