[Term]
id: GSSO:000255
name: punk subculture
def: "A diverse array of ideologies, fashion, and other forms of expression, visual art, dance, literature and film largely characterized by anti-establishment views and the promotion of individual freedom, centred on a loud, aggressive genre of rock music called punk rock." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punk_subculture
is_a: GSSO:000246 ! musical subculture
property_value: wiki:Q1823134 "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85109126" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: GSSO:000256
name: queercore
def: "A cultural and social movement that began in the mid-1980s as an offshoot of the punk subculture. It is distinguished by its discontent with society in general, and specifically society's disapproval of the LGBTQ community. Queercore expresses itself in a D.I.Y. style through magazines, music, writing and film." []
synonym: "homocore" RELATED []
