[Term]
id: GSSO:000258
name: ball culture
def: "An underground LGBTQ subculture that originated in the United States, in which people \"walk\" (i.e., compete) for trophies, prizes, and glory at events known as balls. Ball participants are mainly young Black and Latina members of the LGBTQ community. Attendees can spectate, dance, vogue, and/or walk in one or more of the numerous drag categories that are designed to emulate other genders and social classes, while offering a sort of escape from reality. This culture extends beyond the extravagant events as most participants in ball culture belong to groups known as \"houses\" that mimic a family structure and offer similar support." []
synonym: "ballroom community" RELATED [] {RELATED="house-ballroom community"}
synonym: "house culture" RELATED []
synonym: "house system" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ball_culture
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Ball_culture
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q28130022
