[Term]
id: GSSO:000392
name: aversive therapy by electric shock
def: "Aversive therapy which pairs behavior with electric shocks of mild to higher intensities." []
comment: Aversive therapy by electric shock has been, mostly historically, used in attempts to painfully "convert" gay persons to heterosexuality and transgender persons to being cisgender (despite a lack of evidence of the possibility or efficacy of such a process).
