[Term]
id: GSSO:000404
name: androgyne
def: "A person who identifies as an androgyne." []
comment: Contemporarily, "androgyne" is used as a non-binary gender identity associated to variable extent with androgyny or androgynous expression. Androgynes may describe their gender as simultaneously masculine and feminine.
comment: The origin of the term androgyne in English is multifaceted, being both a borrowing from the Latin androgynus and the French androgyne (itself derived from the Latin androgynus). The Latin form appears to have originated from the ancient Greek ᾰ̓νδρόγῠνος (andrógunos), a combination of the prefix ἀνήρ (anḗr, "man") and the suffix γυνή (gunḗ, "woman").
synonym: "androgyne gender identity" RELATED [] {schema:alternateName="androgyne gender identities"}
synonym: "androgyne person" RELATED [] {schema:alternateName="androgyne persons", schema:alternateName="androgyne people"}
synonym: "femandrogyne" NARROW [] {schema:alternateName="femandrogynes"}
xref: https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/androgyne#English
xref: https://lgbta.fandom.com/wiki/Androgyne
xref: https://mogai-genders.fandom.com/wiki/Androgyne
xref: https://nonbinary.wiki/wiki/Androgyne
