[Term]
id: GSSO:000908
name: natural selection
def: "The differential survival and reproduction of individuals due to differences in phenotype. It is a key mechanism of evolution, the change in the heritable traits characteristic of a population over generations." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_selection
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q43478
is_a: GSSO:000907 ! evolutionary process

[Term]
id: GSSO:000909
name: sexual selection
def: "A mode of natural selection where members of one biological sex choose mates of the other sex to mate with (intersexual selection), and compete with members of the same sex for access to members of the opposite sex (intrasexual selection)." []
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q206913
is_a: GSSO:000908 ! natural selection
property_value: terms:isReferencedBy https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0901132106

[Term]
id: GSSO:000910
name: intersexual selection
def: "A mode of sexual selection in which members of one biological sex choose mates of the other sex to mate with." []
is_a: GSSO:000909 ! sexual selection

[Term]
id: GSSO:000911
name: intrasexual selection
def: "A mode of sexual selection in which members of one biological sex compete with members of the same sex for access to members of the opposite sex." []
is_a: GSSO:000909 ! sexual selection

