xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q160894
is_a: GSSO:001024 ! European ethnic group
property_value: schema:alternateName "Spaniards" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:001034
name: Bengali
def: "An Indo-Aryan ethnic group native to the Bengal region in South Asia, specifically in the eastern part of the Indian subcontinent, presently divided between Bangladesh and the Indian states of West Bengal, Tripura, Assam's Barak Valley, who speak Bengali, a language from the Indo-Aryan language family." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bengalis
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q402913
is_a: GSSO:001029 ! Asian ethnic group
property_value: schema:alternateName "Bengalis" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:001035
name: Russian
def: "An East Slavic ethnic group and nation native to European Russia and other parts of Eastern Europe (some territories of the former Tsardom of Russia and Russian Empire), the most numerous ethnic group in Europe. The majority of ethnic Russians live in the Russian Federation, notable minorities exist in other former Soviet states such as Belarus, Kazakhstan, Moldova, Ukraine and the Baltic states." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russians
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q49542
is_a: GSSO:001024 ! European ethnic group
property_value: schema:alternateName "Russians" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:001036
name: German
def: "A Germanic ethnic group native to Central Europe, who share a common German ancestry, culture and history. German is the shared mother tongue of a substantial majority of ethnic Germans." []
