is_a: GSSO:001207 ! group behavior

[Term]
id: GSSO:001210
name: social facilitation
def: "Any enhancement of a motivated behavior in which individuals do the same thing with some degree of mutual stimulation and consequent coordination." []
def: "Improvement in individual performance when working with other people rather than alone. Compared to their performance when alone, when in the presence of others, they tend to perform better on simple or well-rehearsed tasks and worse on complex or new ones." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_facilitation
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_facilitation_in_animals
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1535412
