[Term]
id: GSSO:001247
name: paraphilic disorder
def: "Disorders that include recurrent, intense sexually arousing fantasies, sexual urges, or behaviors generally involving nonhuman objects, suffering of oneself or partners, or children or other nonconsenting partners." []
comment: The American Psychiatric Association notes that most atypical sexual interests, while possibly considered paraphilic, do not constitute a mental health problem and thus are not considered paraphilic disorders. For example, in a paraphilic disorder, the psychological distress one feels about their paraphilic desire must be distinct from the general societal or cultural disapproval of such a desire.
synonym: "other paraphilic disorder involving non-consenting individuals" NARROW [] {schema:alternateName="other paraphilic disorders involving non-consenting individuals"}
synonym: "other specified paraphilic disorder" NARROW [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Other_specified_paraphilic_disorder] {Property:P1930="302.89"}
synonym: "paraphilia-related disorder" RELATED [] {schema:alternateName="paraphilia-related disorders"}
synonym: "paraphilias and paraphilic disorders" BROAD []
synonym: "paraphilic disorder involving solitary behavior or consenting individuals" NARROW [] {schema:alternateName="paraphilic disorders involving solitary behavior or consenting individuals"}
synonym: "unspecified paraphilic disorder" NARROW [] {schema:alternateName="unspecified paraphilic disorders", Property:P1930="302.9", EXACT="paraphilic disorder, unspecified", RELATED="paraphilic disorders, unspecified"}
