[Term]
id: GSSO:001380
name: queer heterosexuality
def: "Heterosexual practices that are controversially called queer." []
comment: It should be noted that bisexual, pansexual, and transgender people engaging in heterosexual relationships have not "lost" queerness and are still queer persons, even if their relationships may not be.
comment: The term is considered by many LGBTQ people to be offensive because, among other things, it is a misappropriation of the struggles and oppression faced by LGBTQ people, by those who have never experienced this oppression.
