[Term]
id: GSSO:001509
name: sequential hermaphroditism
def: "A type of hermaphroditism that occurs in many fish, gastropods, and plants. Sequential hermaphroditism occurs when the individual changes its sex at some point in its life. In particular, a sequential hermaphrodite produces eggs (female gametes) and sperm (male gametes) at different stages in life. Species that can undergo these changes from one sex to another do so as a normal event within their reproductive cycle that is usually cued by either social structure or the achievement of a certain age or size." []
synonym: "sequential hermaphrodite" RELATED [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermaphrodite#Sequential_hermaphrodites]
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sequential_hermaphroditism
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1209454
is_a: GSSO:001506 ! hermafrodittisme

[Term]
id: GSSO:001510
name: simultaneous hermaphroditism
def: "Hermaphroditism in which an adult organism has functional male and female sexual organs at the same time; often this allows for self-fertilization." []
synonym: "simultaneous hermaphrodite" RELATED [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermaphrodite#Simultaneous_hermaphrodites]
is_a: GSSO:001506 ! hermafrodittisme
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "synchronous hermaphroditism" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:001511
name: protandry
def: "Sequential hermaphroditism in which the animal develops as male, but can later reproduce as female." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sequential_hermaphroditism#Protandry
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q21282742
