[Term]
id: GSSO:001521
name: 47,XXY syndrome
def: "A chromosomal syndrome caused by the presence of an extra X chromosome in the male karyotype. Affected individuals are infertile and have a small penis and testes. They tend to have tall stature and long legs and may have difficulties with speech and language development. Gynecomastia may be present." []
synonym: "47 XXY syndrome" EXACT []
synonym: "47, XXY syndrome" EXACT []
