[Term]
id: GSSO:001534
name: Swyer syndrome
def: "A type of hypogonadism in a person whose karyotype is 46,XY. People with Swyer syndrome are born with the appearance of a normal female in most anatomic respects except that the child has nonfunctional streak gonads instead of ovaries or testes. As their ovaries produce no important body changes before puberty, a defect of the reproductive system typically remains unsuspected until puberty fails to occur. They appear to be normal women and are generally considered so." []
comment: Not to be confused with Swyer-James syndrome.
is_a: GSSO:001520 ! chromosomal intersex condition
is_a: GSSO:012485 ! allosomal chromosomal syndrome
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "Swyer's syndrome" xsd:string
property_value: Property:P138 https://viaf.org/viaf/250593840
