[Term]
id: GSSO:001585
name: progestin-induced virilization
def: "Virilization induced by maternal use of androgens or high doses of certain weakly androgenic synthetic progestogens (progestins) structurally related to testosterone can masculinize (virilize) the external genitalia of a female fetus during susceptible times in pregnancy." []
synonym: "progestin induced virilization" EXACT []
