[Term]
id: GSSO:001756
name: unisex name
def: "A given name that can be used by a person regardless of their gender. Unisex names are common in the English speaking world, especially in the United States. By contrast, some countries have laws preventing unisex names, requiring parents to give their children sex-specific names. In other countries, unisex names are sometimes avoided for social reasons such as potential discrimination, ridicule, and psychological abuse." []
synonym: "androgynous name" RELATED [] {schema:alternateName="androgynous names"}
synonym: "epicene name" RELATED [] {schema:alternateName="epicene names"}
synonym: "gender-neutral name" RELATED [] {schema:alternateName="gender-neutral names"}
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unisex_name
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3409032
is_a: SIO:000181 ! first name
property_value: schema:alternateName "unisex names" xsd:string

