[Term]
id: GSSO:001762
name: drag queen {terms:isReferencedBy="https://web.archive.org/web/20190123175918/https://oramrefugee.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/Glossary-PDF.pdf"}
name: drag queen
name: dragqueen {xref="https://lgbt.dk/ordbog/dragqueen/"}
name: فتى استعراضي
def: "Performance artists, almost always male, who dress in women's clothing and often act with exaggerated femininity and in feminine gender roles with a primarily entertaining purpose. They often exaggerate make-up such as eyelashes for dramatic, comedic or satirical effect. Drag queens are closely associated with gay men and gay culture, but can be of any sexual orientation or gender identity. They vary widely by class, culture, and dedication, from professionals who star in films to people who try drag very occasionally." []
