[Term]
id: GSSO:001875
name: compulsive behavior
def: "The behavior of performing an act persistently and repetitively without it leading to reward or pleasure. The act is usually a small, circumscribed behavior, almost ritualistic, yet not pathologically disturbing. Examples of compulsive behavior include twirling of hair, checking something constantly, not wanting pennies in change, straightening tilted pictures, etc." []
synonym: "abnormal compulsive behavior" RELATED [] {Property:P5806="http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/SNOMEDCT/130972005"}
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compulsive_behavior
