[Term]
id: GSSO:002019
name: binary gender system
def: "The gender binary is the classification of sex and gender into two distinct, opposite and disconnected forms of masculine and feminine." []
comment: It is important to note that the idea of gender binarism is a social construction, not a biological one, per se. Many cultures have more than two gender roles entwined in their respective societies.
synonym: "binarismo de género" RELATED [] {terms:isReferencedBy="https://web.archive.org/web/20200102232435/lgbthealtheducation.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/National-LGBT-Health-Education-Center-Glossary.SPANISH-2018.pdf"}
