[Term]
id: GSSO:002164
name: agule
def: "A gender or social role observed among the Lugbara; the word translates literally as \"like men\" and is used to refer to infertile, prepubertal and postmenopausal women as well as those who do not engage in sexual intercourse with their husbands or other men. Such non-sexuality is associated with the ability to act as a medium for spirits." []
comment: "Agule" is used to describe the sky spirit Adro as the spirit is never ascribed gender.
comment: The term "agule" has been translated as meaning "like a man" in the Lugbara language.
