[Term]
id: GSSO:002189
name: baklâ
name: bayot
def: "A Filipino identity which is considered nonnormative in terms of gender and/or sexuality. Depending on the context, such a person may also consider themselves to be gay, transgender, bisexual, or otherwise part of a cultural gender identity exclusive to the Philippines. However, the term is almost always applied to persons assigned male at birth." []
comment: The argot utilized by the baklâ is called swardspeak, sometimes called gayspeak.
comment: The baklâ identity precedes colonization of the Philippines. Such persons were often held in high regard, being spiritual leaders sometimes called babaylan and katalonan.
