[Term]
id: GSSO:002225
name: political ideology
def: "An ethical set of ideals, principles, doctrines, myths, or symbols of a social movement, institution, class, or large group that explains how society should work, and offers some political and cultural blueprint for a certain social order." []
comment: A political ideology has two dimensions: goals (how society should work) and methods (the most appropriate ways to achieve the ideal arrangement).
