[Term]
id: GSSO:002245
name: liberal feminism
def: "An individualistic form of feminist theory, which focuses on women's ability to maintain their equality through their own actions and choices. Liberal feminists argue that society holds the false belief that women are, by nature, less intellectually and physically capable than men; thus it tends to discriminate against women in the academy, the forum, and the marketplace." []
synonym: "egalitarian feminism" RELATED []
synonym: "mainstream feminism" RELATED []
synonym: "reformist feminism" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Liberal_feminism
