[Term]
id: GSSO:002302
name: fa'afāfine
def: "A gender role and/or identity that is part of Samoan culture. Typically, it refers to persons who are assigned male at birth and who embody both masculine and feminine traits to some degree. Such persons may characterize themselves as transgender women, cisgender gay men, or a distinctly different category of experience." []
comment: The word fa'afafine includes the causative prefix fa'a–, meaning "in the manner of", and the word fafine, meaning "woman".
synonym: "fa'afafine" EXACT []
