[Term]
id: GSSO:002305
name: hijra
name: هجرة
name: हिजड़ा
name: হিজড়া
def: "A gender role observed in many communities on the Indian subcontinent. Many hijras also consider themselves to be transgender women or intersex persons, but the concept predates that terminology. Hijra are almost exclusively assigned male at birth and some undergo an initiation ritual called nirwaan (nirvan), which involves removal of the penis, scrotum, and testicles." []
comment: Hijras tend to reside in somewhat intentional communities, being ostensibly separate from other Indian gender and sexual minorities. They engage in specific rituals and professions and utilize an argot known as Hijra Farsi, which is a blend of Persian and Hindustani.
comment: Note that hijra who might "fit" the designation of transgender woman may not identify as such, and will thus not be filed under both designations. Further, not all Indian, Pakistani, and Bengali transgender women are hijra, and thus will not be included in this categorization.
comment: The term "hijra" is sometimes considered offensive in Pakistan, with the Urdu خواجه سرا‎ (khwaja sara) being preferred.
comment: The word hijra has historically been translated into English as "eunuch" or "hermaphrodite" but this contextualization is both inappropriate and inaccurate.
synonym: "GSSO:006190" RELATED []
synonym: "GSSO:006199" RELATED []
synonym: "hijrā" EXACT []
synonym: "हिजड़ों" RELATED []
