[Term]
id: GSSO:002309
name: kothi
name: कोथी
name: কোতি
def: "A heterogeneous gender role or categorization of the Indian subcontinent. Typically used to refer to persons assigned male at birth who take on a passive role in sexual relationships with other men (analogous to the idea of a \"bottom\" in many English-speaking countries)." []
comment: Kothi differ significantly from hijra in that the former do not live in intentional communities as hijra often do. However, some hijra identify as kothi and vice versa.
comment: Note that some kothi identify as bisexual or pansexual, not necessarily as exclusively gay.
