[Term]
id: GSSO:002312
name: meti
def: "A Nepali word with no direct translation in English; it is often used to refer to transgender women or other persons assigned female at birth with expression of some female gender identity; however, it can also be used to refer to cross-dressers, hijra, and feminine cisgender gay men." []
def: "An equivalent identity to kothi observed in Nepal." []
comment: Some articles offensively translate "meti" as "berdache", a pejorative colonialist term used by Europeans to describe nonnormative gender roles in Native American and First Nation communities. This use is extremely inappropriate.
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meti_(gender)
