[Term]
id: GSSO:002360
name: eugenic theory
def: "A set of beliefs and practices that aim to improve the genetic quality of a human population by excluding (through a variety of morally criticized means) certain genetic groups judged to be inferior, and promoting other genetic groups judged to be superior." []
comment: The concept predates the term; Plato suggested applying the principles of selective breeding to humans around 400 BC. Early advocates of eugenics in the 19th century regarded it as a way of improving groups of people. In contemporary usage, the term eugenics is closely associated with scientific racism.
synonym: "eugenic" RELATED []
synonym: "negative eugenics" NARROW []
synonym: "positive eugenics" NARROW []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Eugenics
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eugenics
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q170480
is_a: GSSO:012661 ! pseudobiological theory
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "eugenics" xsd:string
property_value: Property:P1149 "HQ750-HQ755.5" xsd:string
property_value: Property:P3938 "Francis Galton" xsd:string {dc:date="1883"}
property_value: Property:P486 "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D005053" xsd:anyURI
