[Term]
id: GSSO:002390
name: LGBTQ history
def: "A branch of social history which studies instances of lesbian, gay, bisexual, and transgender behavior and peoples throughout different cultures, with special regard to the persecution of such people. It also includes history of third gender roles and identities, history of intersex peoples, history of asexual individuals, and other related gender and sexual identities." []
