[Term]
id: GSSO:002406
name: personal pronoun
def: "A pronoun that is associated primarily with a particular grammatical person – first person (as I), second person (as you), or third person (as he, she, it, they). Personal pronouns may also take different forms depending on number (usually singular or plural), grammatical or natural gender, case, and formality." []
comment: The term "personal" is used here purely to signify the grammatical sense; personal pronouns are not limited to people and can also refer to animals and objects (as the English personal pronoun it usually does).
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Personal_pronouns
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Personal_pronoun
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q468801
