[Term]
id: GSSO:002824
name: cognitive bias
def: "A systematic pattern of deviation from norm or rationality in judgment. Individuals create their own \"subjective social reality\" from their perception of the input. An individual's construction of social reality, not the objective input, may dictate their behaviour in the social world. Thus, cognitive biases may sometimes lead to perceptual distortion, inaccurate judgment, illogical interpretation, or what is broadly called irrationality." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Cognitive_biases
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cognitive_bias
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_cognitive_biases
is_a: GSSO:002822 ! bias
property_value: Property:P5191 GSSO:002822
property_value: schema:alternateName "cognitive biases" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:002825
name: contextual bias
def: "Biases which occur when a person is influenced by extraneous information." []
is_a: GSSO:002822 ! bias
property_value: Property:P5191 GSSO:002822
property_value: schema:alternateName "contextual biases" xsd:string

[Term]
