[Term]
id: GSSO:002861
name: homofobi {xref="https://lgbt.dk/ordbog/homofobi/"}
name: homofobi {terms:isReferencedBy="https://web.archive.org/web/20190123175918/https://oramrefugee.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/Glossary-PDF.pdf"}
name: homofobia {terms:isReferencedBy="https://web.archive.org/web/20200102232435/lgbthealtheducation.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/National-LGBT-Health-Education-Center-Glossary.SPANISH-2018.pdf"}
name: homophobia
name: homophobie {terms:isReferencedBy="https://web.archive.org/web/20190123175918/https://oramrefugee.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/Glossary-PDF.pdf"}
def: "A range of negative attitudes and feelings toward homosexuality and gay people. It has been defined as contempt, prejudice, aversion, hatred or antipathy, may be based on irrational fear and ignorance, and is often related to religious beliefs." []
comment: Homophobia is sometimes used as a "catch-all" term for forms of LGBTQIA+ prejudice.
comment: In the 1990s, behavioral scientists William O'Donohue and Christine Caselles argued that the term homophobia was pejorative. In 2012, the Associated Press Stylebook was revised to advise against using -phobia words in non-clinical ways, and AP editor Dave Minthorn suggested replacing "homophobic" with "anti-gay".
synonym: "gaycism" RELATED []
synonym: "homoerotophobia" NARROW [] {RELATED="homoerotophobic"}
synonym: "homomismia" RELATED []
synonym: "homophobic" RELATED []
synonym: "homophobism" RELATED []
