[Term]
id: GSSO:002937
name: economic ideology
def: "An ideology which expresses perspectives on the way an economy should run and to what end." []
comment: An economic ideology is different from an economic theory in that it is normative rather than just explanatory in its approach. An economic theory aims to create accurate explanatory models to describe how an economy currently functions.
comment: An economic ideology is distinct from an economic system (such as a market economy) to the extent that explaining an economic system (positive economics) is distinct from advocating it (normative economics).
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Economic_ideologies
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economic_ideology
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5333510
