[Term]
id: GSSO:002968
name: white privilege
def: "The societal privilege that benefits white people over non-white people, particularly if they are otherwise under the same social, political, or economic circumstances. With roots in European colonialism, the spread of the British Empire, and the enactment of the Atlantic slave trade, white privilege has developed over centuries, in circumstances that have broadly sought to protect white racial privileges, various national citizenships and other rights or special benefits." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:White_privilege
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_privilege
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q17016489
