[Term]
id: GSSO:002974
name: Christian privilege
def: "Any of several advantages bestowed upon Christians in some societies. This arises out of the presumption that Christian belief is a social norm, that leads to the marginalization of the nonreligious and members of other religions through institutional religious discrimination or religious persecution. Christian privilege can also lead to the neglect of outsiders' cultural heritage and religious practices." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_privilege
is_a: GSSO:002972 ! religious privilege

[Term]
id: GSSO:002975
name: body privilege
