[Term]
id: GSSO:003012
name: gendered violence
def: "The term used to denote harm inflicted upon individuals and groups that is connected to normative understandings of their gender. This connection can be in the form of cultural understandings of gender roles, both institutional and structural forces that endorse violence based on gender and societal influences that shape violent events along gender lines. While the term is often used synonymously with ‘violence against women’, gendered violence can and does occur for people of all genders including men, women, male and female children and gender diverse individuals." []
synonym: "gender identity-related violence" NARROW [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Gender_identity_related_violence]
synonym: "sexual and gender-based violence" BROAD [] {Property:P1813="SGBV"}
synonym: "violence by gender" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Gender-related_violence
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gender_violence
