[Term]
id: GSSO:003015
name: persecutive violence
def: "The systematic mistreatment of an individual or group by another individual or group. The most common forms are religious persecution, racism and political persecution, though there is naturally some overlap between these terms. The inflicting of suffering, harassment, imprisonment, internment, fear, or pain are all factors that may establish persecution, but not all suffering will necessarily establish persecution." []
synonym: "persecution" RELATED [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Persecution, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persecution, https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q851824] {wiki:Q1823134="http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85100050"}
synonym: "persecutive behavior" RELATED []
is_a: GSSO:012171 ! violence by type
property_value: Property:P5191 NCIT:C93214

