[Term]
id: GSSO:003199
name: gender essentialism
def: "A concept used to examine the attribution of fixed, intrinsic, innate qualities to women and men. In this theory, there are certain universal, innate, biologically- or psychologically-based features of gender (different from sex) that are at the root of observed differences in the behavior of men and women." []
synonym: "gender essence" RELATED []
synonym: "gender essentialist" RELATED []
synonym: "gendered essence" RELATED []
xref: https://lgbtqia.fandom.com/wiki/Gender_essentialism
is_a: GSSO:003200 ! biological essentialism
property_value: Property:P5191 NCIT:C17357
property_value: seeAlso GSSO:011949
property_value: terms:isReferencedBy http://web.archive.org/web/20201115050831/https://www.translanguageprimer.org/primer

[Term]
id: GSSO:003200
name: biological essentialism
def: "Belief that some part of human nature or some personal characteristic (such as intelligence, homosexuality, gender presentation, etc.) are innate and have some \"natural essence\", rather than being a social construction." []
