[Term]
id: GSSO:003551
name: radical lesbian feminism
def: "A lesbian movement that challenges the status quo of heterosexuality and mainstream feminism. It arose in part because mainstream feminism did not actively include or fight for lesbian rights. The movement was started by lesbian feminist groups in the United States in the 1950s and 1960s. A Canadian movement followed in the 1970s, which added momentum. As it continued to gain popularity, radical lesbianism spread throughout Canada, the United States, and France." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radical_feminism#Radical_lesbian_feminism
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radical_lesbianism
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3182288
