[Term]
id: GSSO:003554
name: gender critical feminism
def: "A form of radical feminism (although this is highly debated) which purports to be based upon a critical reading or definition of what gender is or is seen to be, thus basing particular criteria on womanhood or what a \"real\" woman is. Such ideologies are almost always transphobic and used to exclude transgender women from women's spaces, among other things." []
comment: Oftentimes this term is a misnormer applied to conservative anti-feminist anti-gender movements.
synonym: "gender conservative feminism" RELATED []
synonym: "gender critical activism" RELATED []
synonym: "gender-critical feminism" EXACT []
is_a: GSSO:003553 ! transgender-exclusionary radical feminism
property_value: Property:P1813 "GCism" xsd:string
property_value: Property:P1813 "gender critical" xsd:string {schema:alternateName="gender criticals"}
