is_a: GSSO:003619 ! masculinity by level

[Term]
id: GSSO:003625
name: feminine essence theory
def: "The concept that transgender women are women trapped in men's bodies. This idea has been interpreted in many senses, as a female mind, spirit, soul, personality, etc., as well as in more literal senses such as having a female brain structure; it is also a psychological narrative, that is, a self-description of how some transgender women see themselves, or of how they may portray themselves to qualify for certain medical treatments." []
synonym: "feminine essence" RELATED []
synonym: "feminine essence concept" RELATED []
synonym: "feminine essence narrative" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feminine_essence_concept_of_transsexuality
is_a: GSSO:003199 ! gender essentialism

[Term]
id: GSSO:003626
name: situational sexual behavior
def: "Situational sexual behavior differs from that which the person normally exhibits, due to a social environment that in some way permits, encourages, or compels the behavior in question. This can also include situations where a person's usual sexual behavior may not be possible, so rather than not engaging in sexual activity at all, they may engage in different sexual behaviors." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Situational_sexual_behavior
