[Term]
id: GSSO:003682
name: liberty
def: "The ability to do as one pleases. In modern politics, liberty is the state of being free within society from oppressive restrictions imposed by authority on one's way of life, behavior, or political views. In philosophy, liberty involves free will as contrasted with determinism. In theology, liberty is freedom from the effects of \"sin, spiritual servitude, [or] worldly ties\"." []
