[Term]
id: GSSO:003758
name: philosophy of mind
def: "A branch of philosophy that studies the ontology and nature of the mind and its relationship with the body. The mind–body problem is a paradigm issue in philosophy of mind, although other issues are addressed, such as the hard problem of consciousness, and the nature of particular mental states." []
synonym: "metaphysics of mind" RELATED [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Metaphysics_of_mind]
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Philosophy_of_mind
