[Term]
id: GSSO:003761
name: other identity
def: "The other human being in their differences from the self, as being a cumulative, constituting factor in the self-image of a person; as acknowledgement of being real. Usually, the \"other\" is used in relationship to the quality of \"otherness\", he state of being different from and alien to the social identity of a person and to the identity of the self. To \"other\" someone (as a verb) is to reduce them by labeling and defining them as a subaltern native, as someone who belongs to the socially subordinate category of the other." []
synonym: "alterity" RELATED [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alterity, https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q583580]
synonym: "Other" EXACT []
synonym: "othering" RELATED [] {EXACT="Othering"}
synonym: "otherness" RELATED [] {EXACT="Otherness"}
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Other_(philosophy)
