[Term]
id: GSSO:003762
name: youth subculture
def: "A youth-based subculture with distinct styles, behaviors, and interests. Youth subcultures offer participants an identity outside of that ascribed by social institutions such as family, work, home and school. Youth subcultures that show a systematic hostility to the dominant culture are sometimes described as countercultures." []
synonym: "youth-based subculture" RELATED []
