[Term]
id: GSSO:003792
name: pink
def: "A pale tint of red that is named after a flower of the same name. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. According to surveys in Europe and the United States, pink is the color most often associated with charm, politeness, sensitivity, tenderness, sweetness, childhood, femininity and romance. A combination of pink and white is associated with chastity and innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction." []
def: "Any of a group of colors reddish in hue, of medium to high lightness, and of low to moderate saturation." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Pink
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q429220
