[Term]
id: GSSO:003814
name: market economy
def: "An economic system in which the decisions regarding investment, production and distribution are guided by the price signals created by the forces of supply and demand. The major characteristic of a market economy is the existence of factor markets that play a dominant role in the allocation of capital and the factors of production." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Market_economy
is_a: GSSO:003812 ! economic system
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "laissez-faire capitalism" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:003815
name: mixed economy
def: "An economic system blending elements of market economies with elements of planned economies, free markets with state interventionism, or private enterprise with public enterprise." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mixed_economy
is_a: GSSO:003812 ! economic system

[Term]
id: GSSO:003816
name: planned economy
def: "A type of economic system where investment, production and the allocation of capital goods take place according to economy-wide economic plans and production plans." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planned_economy
is_a: GSSO:003812 ! economic system

[Term]
id: GSSO:003817
name: capitalism
def: "An economic ideology which posits private ownership of the means of production and their operation for profit in the form of a capitalist market economy. Additionally, capitalism suggests that decision-making and investments are determined by every owner of wealth, property or production ability in financial and capital markets, whereas prices and the distribution of goods and services are mainly determined by competition in goods and services markets." []
synonym: "capitalist" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capitalism
