[Term]
id: GSSO:003858
name: second-wave feminism
def: "A period of feminist activity and thought that began in the United States in the early 1960s and lasted roughly two decades. It quickly spread across the Anglo-European world, with an aim to increase equality for women by gaining more than just enfranchisement." []
synonym: "second wave feminism" EXACT []
