[Term]
id: GSSO:003859
name: third-wave feminism
def: "An iteration of the feminist movement that began in the early 1990s United States and continued until the rise of the fourth wave in the 2010s. Born in the 1960s and 1970s as members of Generation X and grounded in the civil-rights advances of the second wave, third-wave feminists embraced individualism and diversity and sought to redefine what it meant to be a feminist." []
synonym: "third wave feminism" EXACT []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Third-wave_feminism
