[Term]
id: GSSO:003860
name: fourth-wave feminism
def: "A phase of feminism that began around 2012 and is characterized by a focus on the empowerment of women and the use of internet tools. Centered on intersectionality, the fourth wave examines the interlocking systems of power that contribute to the stratification of traditionally marginalized groups. Fourth-wave feminists advocate for greater representation of these groups in politics and business, and argue that society would be more equitable if policies and practices incorporated the perspectives of all people." []
synonym: "fourth wave feminism" EXACT []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Fourth-wave_feminism
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourth-wave_feminism
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q25382187
is_a: GSSO:003856 ! feminism by wave
property_value: Property:P5191 GSSO:002229
property_value: wiki:Q1823134 "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2021008241" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: GSSO:003861
name: fifth-wave feminism
def: "A theoretical next wave of feminism which encourages a disconnect between the ideal of a \"modern woman\" and that person's identity as a modern woman." []
