[Term]
id: GSSO:003955
name: transmedicalism
def: "A term covering a wide range of transphobic beliefs held by some members of the transgender community. These beliefs essentially distinguish between \"true\" transgender people (those who experience gender dysphoria, take or will take hormones as part of hormone replacement therapy, and have or will undergo gender confirmation surgery). One of transmedicalism's central beliefs is that gender dysphoria is a medical condition which requires HRT and GCS as treatment and that anyone who says they are trans and does not have dysphoria or does not want HRT or GCS is a \"transtrender\" or part of a fad." []
synonym: "transfundamentalism" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transmedicalism
