[Term]
id: GSSO:003967
name: hybrid masculinity
def: "A theoretical concept that describes the use of aspects of marginalized gender expressions in the gender performance or identity of privileged men. Scholarship on hybrid masculinities suggests that they simultaneously distance themselves from traditional norms of masculinity while reproducing and reinforcing hegemonic masculinity." []
