[Term]
id: GSSO:003969
name: inclusive masculinity
def: "An approach to thinking about masculinity in the context of social changes that have undermined traditional hegemonic masculinity and its associated homophobia, which each have driven men to avoid certain behaviors in order to avoid being publicly perceived as gay; it holds that there are increasingly societal spaces in which men no longer need to behave in hypermasculine ways in order to be accepted." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inclusive_masculinity
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q24963110
