[Term]
id: GSSO:004179
name: anatomical sex
def: "Sex designation classified purely, or mostly, based on an individual's apparent physical sex characteristics, particularly genitalia." []
comment: Anatomical sex can sometimes be non-specific. If external genitalia are present but not internal sex organs, for instance. More specific terms, or noting of organ presence/absence are usually more appropriate in medical contexts.
comment: Typically, anatomical sex aligns with the concept of sex assigned at birth, although this isn't always the case, especially when considering any of various anatomical intersex conditions.
synonym: "external anatomical sex" NARROW []
synonym: "GSSO:000105" RELATED []
synonym: "internal anatomical sex" NARROW []
synonym: "physical sex" RELATED []
