[Term]
id: GSSO:004240
name: cisgender
name: cisgenre {terms:isReferencedBy="GSSO:011927", terms:isReferencedBy="https://web.archive.org/web/20190123175918/https://oramrefugee.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/Glossary-PDF.pdf"}
name: cisgênero {terms:isReferencedBy="https://web.archive.org/web/20210121145426/https://nonbinary.wiki/wiki/Glossary_of_Brazilian_Portuguese_gender_and_sex_terminology"}
name: ciskønnet {xref="https://lgbt.dk/ordbog/ciskoennet/"}
name: na-trans {terms:isReferencedBy="https://web.archive.org/web/20190123175918/https://oramrefugee.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/Glossary-PDF.pdf"}
def: "Having a gender (identity) which matches the sex one was assigned at birth; or, pertaining to such people." []
def: "The word \"cisgender\" was first published in the third edition of the Oxford English Dictionary (OED) in June 2015." []
synonym: "cis-gender" EXACT []
synonym: "cisgender and cissexual" BROAD []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cisgender
xref: https://lgbt.wikia.org/wiki/Cisgender
xref: https://lgbta.fandom.com/wiki/Cisgender
xref: https://lgbtq-wiki.fandom.com/wiki/Cisgender
xref: https://lgbtqia.fandom.com/wiki/Cisgender
xref: https://nonbinary.wiki/wiki/Cisgender
is_a: GSSO:012491 ! non-transgender gender modality
property_value: dc:identifier "https://lgbtq-language-project.appspot.com/#cisgender" xsd:anyURI
property_value: dc:identifier "https://mamoura.eci.ufmg.br/tematres/vocab/index.php?tema=20" xsd:anyURI {terms:source="GSSO:010941"}
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "cisgender (cis)" xsd:string
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "cisgender or cis" xsd:string
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "non-transgender" xsd:string {EXACT="nontransgender", RELATED="nontrans", Property:P1813="non-trans"}
property_value: Property:P1683 "As for the origin [of the word \"cisgendered\"]; I just made it up. I just kept running into the problem of what to call non-T*people in various discussions, and one day it just hit me: non-trans = cis. Therefore, cisgendered." xsd:string {terms:source="https://web.archive.org/web/20181014052058/https://groups.google.com/forum/message/raw?msg=soc.support.transgendered/uQOv7egWih0/Y4nkFd9QSBgJ"}
property_value: Property:P1683 "I am trying to assess campus climates for the transgender community, both at my own institution and at other campuses. Any information regarding this subject would be tremendously helpful to this effort. Personal testimony, activism, organizations, experience of providers and human service workers, etc. Issues of interest are transphobia, hostility, general knowledge and understanding, attitudes of the queer community and cisgendered people, etc. I am interested in building coalitions and will share any info with others." xsd:string {terms:source="https://web.archive.org/web/20181014051630/https://groups.google.com/forum/message/raw?msg=alt.transgendered/acBONWZqmhs/xo2v8gve62kJ"}
property_value: Property:P1683 "The cisgender world treats us all the same, to them we are just a bunch of drag-fags and thanks to the stupid rules about who wears what, we all get fragged for it.  The little matter that we all crossdress for different reasons is utterly lost on the cisgender world." xsd:string {terms:source="https://web.archive.org/web/20181014045425/https://groups.google.com/forum/message/raw?msg=alt.transgendered/XnSVJnxLWcI/w20uj1ujPAUJ"}
property_value: Property:P1683 "The transgender movement has taken a similar approach to confronting transphobia, by encouraging cisgender people to become comfortable with their own expressions of femininity and/or masculinity in order to be respectful of those expressions in others." xsd:string {terms:source="https://www.worldcat.org/oclc/81252738", schema:pageEnd="91", schema:pageStart="91"}
property_value: Property:P1683 "This group [soc.support.transgendered] may be the form to discuss politics and law, so not getting a responce might be expected here. I wouldn't have even replied to this post accepting that a challenge was  made to the notion it worthless and unsupportive to discuss the differences between each of us and our  labels, whether that be transsexual, homosexual, hetrosexual, transgender, cisgender, transidentity or polymorph or fish..." xsd:string {terms:source="https://web.archive.org/web/20181014050317/https://groups.google.com/forum/message/raw?msg=soc.support.transgendered/GbxctMNUnyw/KTGFMu6ytaEJ"}
property_value: Property:P1813 "cis" xsd:string {terms:isReferencedBy="http://web.archive.org/web/20200107185327/https://www.transgendermap.com/resources/words/slang-slurs/"}
property_value: Property:P1813 "cis" xsd:string {terms:isReferencedBy="GSSO:011927"}
property_value: Property:P1813 "cis" xsd:string {xref="https://lgbt.dk/ordbog/cis/"}
property_value: Property:P461 GSSO:000096
