[Term]
id: GSSO:004386
name: transgender history
def: "Transgender history begins with transgender (in the broad sense, including non-binary and third-gender) people in ancient civilizations on every inhabited continent and continues to the present. Sumerian and Akkadian texts from 4500 years ago document transgender priests, and Assyrian texts document trans prostitutes; evidence suggests these gender roles go back to prehistoric times and may have a common origin with third gender roles that were accepted in America before European colonization, some of which (like Navajo nádleehi and Zuni lhamana) survived colonizers' hostility." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Transgender_history
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transgender_history
