[Term]
id: GSSO:004422
name: psychodynamic complex
def: "A core pattern of emotions, memories, perceptions, and wishes in the personal unconscious organized around a common theme, such as power or status." []
comment: Note that many psychodynamic complexes are poorly defined, pseudoscientific, described mostly in literature, or have been replaced by other clinical psychological/psychiatric terminology.
synonym: "psychological complex" RELATED [] {schema:alternateName="psychological complexes"}
is_a: GSSO:000489 ! mental health condition
