[Term]
id: GSSO:004795
name: anal psychosexual phase
def: "The second stage of psychosexual development is the anal stage, spanning from the age of eighteen months to three years, wherein the infant's erogenous zone changes from the mouth (the upper digestive tract) to the anus (the lower digestive tract), while the ego formation continues." []
is_a: GSSO:004753 ! Freudian phase of psychosexual development
property_value: Property:P5191 http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma15711
property_value: Property:P5806 "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/SNOMEDCT/12136001" xsd:anyURI
property_value: schema:alternateName "anal psychosexual phases" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:004796
name: genital psychosexual phase
def: "The fifth stage of psychosexual development is the genital stage that spans puberty through adult life, and thus represents most of a person's life; its purpose is the psychological detachment and independence from the parents. The genital stage affords the person the ability to confront and resolve his or her remaining psychosexual childhood conflicts." []
is_a: GSSO:004753 ! Freudian phase of psychosexual development
property_value: Property:P5806 "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/SNOMEDCT/69849007" xsd:anyURI
property_value: schema:alternateName "genital psychosexual phases" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:004797
name: latent psychosexual phase
def: "The fourth stage of psychosexual development is the latency stage that spans from the age of six years until puberty, wherein the child consolidates the character habits they developed in the three, earlier stages of psychologic and sexual development." []
is_a: GSSO:004753 ! Freudian phase of psychosexual development
property_value: Property:P5806 "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/SNOMEDCT/472996001" xsd:anyURI
property_value: schema:alternateName "latent psychosexual phases" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:004798
name: oral psychosexual phase
def: "The first stage of psychosexual development is the oral stage, spanning from birth until the age of one year, wherein the infant's mouth is the focus of libidinal gratification derived from the pleasure of feeding at the mother's breast, and from the oral exploration of his or her environment, i.e. the tendency to place objects in the mouth." []
is_a: GSSO:004753 ! Freudian phase of psychosexual development
property_value: Property:P5806 "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/SNOMEDCT/16430000" xsd:anyURI
property_value: schema:alternateName "oral psychosexual phases" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:004799
name: phallic psychosexual phase
def: "The third stage of psychosexual development is the phallic stage, spanning the ages of three to six years, wherein the child's genitalia are his or her primary erogenous zone. It is in this third infantile development stage that children become aware of their bodies, the bodies of other children, and the bodies of their parents; they gratify physical curiosity by undressing and exploring each other and their genitals, and so learn the physical (sexual) differences between \"male\" and \"female\" and the gender differences between \"boy\" and \"girl\"." []
is_a: GSSO:004753 ! Freudian phase of psychosexual development
property_value: Property:P5806 "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/SNOMEDCT/472995002" xsd:anyURI
property_value: schema:alternateName "phallic psychosexual phases" xsd:string

