[Term]
id: GSSO:005272
name: HIV/AIDS denialism
def: "The belief, contradicted by conclusive evidence, that human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) does not cause acquired immune deficiency syndrome (AIDS). Some of its proponents reject the existence of HIV, while others accept that HIV exists but argue that it is a harmless passenger virus and not the cause of AIDS. Insofar as they acknowledge AIDS as a real disease, they attribute it to some combination of sexual behavior, recreational drugs, malnutrition, poor sanitation, haemophilia, or the effects of the drugs used to treat HIV infection (antiretrovirals)." []
synonym: "AIDS denialism" NARROW [] {hasSynonym="AIDS denial"}
synonym: "HIV denialism" NARROW [] {RELATED="HIV denial"}
synonym: "HIV/AIDS denial" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:HIV/AIDS_denialism
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HIV/AIDS_denialism
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1333233
