[Term]
id: GSSO:005320
name: plateau phase
def: "The period of sexual excitement prior to orgasm. The phase is characterised by an increased circulation and heart rate in both sexes, increased sexual pleasure with increased stimulation and further increased muscle tension. Also, respiration continues at an elevated level." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_sexual_response_cycle#Plateau_phase
is_a: GSSO:005317 ! human sexual response cycle phase
property_value: Property:P155 GSSO:005318
property_value: Property:P156 GSSO:005319

[Term]
id: GSSO:005321
name: resolution phase
def: "The phase of the human sexual response cycle which occurs after orgasm and allows the muscles to relax, blood pressure to drop and the body to slow down from its excited state." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_sexual_response_cycle#Resolution_phase
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Refractory_period_(sex)
