[Term]
id: GSSO:005372
name: Manitoba Saulteaux
def: "One of the major divisions of the Saulteaux, found primarily in eastern and southern Manitoba, extending west into southern Saskatchewan. During the late 18th century and early 19th century, as partners with the Cree in the fur trade, the Saulteaux migrated northwest into the Swan River and Cumberland districts of west-central Manitoba, and into Saskatchewan along the Assiniboine River, as far its confluence with the Souris (Mouse) River. Once established in the area, the Saulteaux adapted some of the cultural traits of their allies, the Plains Cree and Assiniboine." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saulteaux#Manitoba_Saulteaux
is_a: GSSO:005371 ! Saulteaux
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "Central Saulteaux" xsd:string

