[Term]
id: GSSO:005377
name: gender cue
def: "A trait or feature one uses in order to attempt to identify a person's gender or sex." []
comment: Gender cues can be culturally bound (such as European women typically wearing longer hairstyles) or more biologically focused (people who were assigned male at birth often develop lower voices). Other examples of gender cues include body movements and gestures and facial hair.
