[Term]
id: GSSO:005478
name: socioeconomic status
def: "An economic and sociological combined total measure of a person's work experience and of an individual's or family's economic and social position in relation to others, based on household income, earners' education, and occupation are examined, as well as combined income, whereas for an individual's SES only their own attributes are assessed. However, SES is more commonly used to depict an economic difference in society as a whole." []
synonym: "socio-economic status" EXACT []
is_a: GSSO:005477 ! social status
