[Term]
id: GSSO:005480
name: middle class
def: "A class of people in the middle of a social hierarchy. However, it is oversimplification to consider this term as an easily identifiable category that falls between \"x\" and \"y\" on one specific, agreed-upon continuum with established criteria. The definition of the term \"middle class\" is highly political and vigorously contested by various schools of political and economic philosophy." []
comment: Modern social theorists—and especially economists—have defined and re-defined the term "middle class" in order to serve their particular social or political ends. The definitions of the term "middle class" therefore are the result of the more- or less-scientific methods used when delineating the parameters of what is and isn't "middle class."
synonym: "bourgeoisie" RELATED [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bourgeoisie, https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q52090] {def="An affluent and often opulent stratum of the middle class who stand opposite the proletariat class."}
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Middle_class
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Middle_class
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q241588
is_a: GSSO:005476 ! social class
property_value: Property:P1149 "HT680-HT690" xsd:string
property_value: Property:P3938 https://viaf.org/viaf/34016737/ {dc:date="1745"}
property_value: wiki:Q1823134 "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85085013" xsd:anyURI

