[Term]
id: GSSO:005483
name: upper middle class
def: "The social group constituted by higher status members of the middle class. This is in contrast to the term lower middle class, which is used for the group at the opposite end of the middle-class stratum, and to the broader term middle class. There is considerable debate as to how the upper middle class might be defined." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Upper_middle_class
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upper_middle_class
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2751085
is_a: GSSO:005480 ! middle class

[Term]
id: GSSO:005484
name: lower middle class
def: "A subdivision of the greater middle class. Usually the term refers to the group of middle class households or individuals who have not attained the status of the upper middle class associated with the higher realms of the middle class." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lower_middle_class
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3269776
is_a: GSSO:005480 ! middle class

