[Term]
id: GSSO:005494
name: Puebloan
def: "Native Americans in the Southwestern United States who share common agricultural, material and religious practices. When Spaniards entered the area beginning in the 16th century, they came across complex, multi-story villages built of adobe, stone and other local materials, which they called pueblos, or villages, a term that later came to refer also to the peoples who live in these villages." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Puebloan_peoples
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puebloans
