property_value: Property:P5806 "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/SNOMEDCT/71949006" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: GSSO:005500
name: Oji-Cree
def: "A First Nation in the Canadian provinces of Ontario and Manitoba, residing in a narrow band extending from the Missinaibi River region in Northeastern Ontario at the east to Lake Winnipeg at the west. The Oji-Cree people are descended from historical intermarriage between the Ojibwa and Cree cultures, but are generally considered a nation distinct from either of their ancestral groups." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oji-Cree
is_a: GSSO:005369 ! Anishinaabe

[Term]
id: GSSO:005501
name: Algonquian
def: "One of the most populous and widespread North American Indigenous language groups. Today, thousands of individuals identify with various Algonquian peoples. Historically, the peoples were prominent along the Atlantic Coast and into the interior along the Saint Lawrence River and around the Great Lakes. This grouping consists of the peoples who speak Algonquian languages." []
xref: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C43879
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algonquian_peoples
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Algonquian_peoples
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1621197
is_a: GSSO:005369 ! Anishinaabe
