[Term]
id: GSSO:005507
name: Cheyenne
def: "One of the Indigenous peoples of the Great Plains that speak a language that is a member of the Algonquian language family. The Cheyenne comprise two Native American tribes, the Só'taeo'o or Só'taétaneo'o (more commonly spelled as Suhtai or Sutaio) and the Tsétsêhéstâhese (also spelled Tsitsistas). These tribes merged in the early 19th century." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheyenne
is_a: GSSO:005501 ! Algonquian
property_value: Property:P1748 "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C43926" xsd:anyURI

