[Term]
id: GSSO:005509
name: Chickasaw
def: "An Indigenous people of the Southeastern Woodlands. Their traditional territory was in the Southeastern United States of Mississippi, Alabama and Tennessee. Their language is classified as a member of the Muskogean language family. In the present day, they are organized as the federally recognized Chickasaw Nation." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chickasaw
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q622728
is_a: GSSO:005508 ! Muskogean

