[Term]
id: GSSO:005682
name: involuntary manslaughter
def: "The homicide of a human being without intent of doing so, either expressed or implied. It is distinguished from voluntary manslaughter by the absence of intention." []
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q118322
is_a: GSSO:005681 ! manslaughter

[Term]
id: GSSO:005683
name: voluntary manslaughter
def: "The killing of a human being in which the offender acted during the heat of passion, under circumstances that would cause a reasonable person to become emotionally or mentally disturbed to the point that they can't reasonably control their emotions." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voluntary_manslaughter
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1295558
is_a: GSSO:005681 ! manslaughter

[Term]
id: GSSO:005684
name: constructive manslaughter
def: "Manslaughter which occurs when someone kills, without intent, in the course of committing an unlawful act. The malice involved in the crime is transferred to the killing, resulting in a charge of manslaughter." []
is_a: GSSO:005682 ! involuntary manslaughter
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "unlawful act manslaughter" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:005685
name: criminally negligent manslaughter
def: "Manslaughter which occurs where death results from serious negligence, or, in some jurisdictions, serious recklessness. A high degree of negligence is required to warrant criminal liability. A related concept is that of willful blindness, which is where a defendant intentionally puts themself in a position where the defendant will be unaware of facts which would render them liable." []
is_a: GSSO:005682 ! involuntary manslaughter
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "criminally negligent homicide" xsd:string {comment="So called in the United States."}
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "gross negligence manslaughter" xsd:string {comment="So called in England and Wales."}

