[Term]
id: GSSO:005766
name: half-and-half
def: "Name given to certain performers in American circus sideshow and carnival circuits during the first half of the 20th century. These performers would often claim to be \"true hermaphrodites\" (intersex individuals), presenting as male on one side of their body and female on the other side of their body. Well-known \"half-and-half\" performers included Josephine Joseph and Bobby Kork." []
synonym: "half and half" EXACT [] {schema:alternateName="half and halfs"}
