[Term]
id: GSSO:005770
name: transformista
def: "A primarily performative cultural identity in many Spanish and Portuguese speaking countries in Central and South America." []
comment: "Transformista" is often translated as "transvestite" in English, which is an inaccurate translation. While "transformist" may be more appropriate, using "transformista" is usually preferred.
comment: The transformista identity predates the emergence of the  American "drag queen" identity in many Central and South American countries. Their performances usually involve specific impersonation of Central and South American "divas" as well as dance and music specific to those cultures.
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q10384150
is_a: GSSO:002194 ! performative cross-dresser
