[Term]
id: GSSO:005936
name: Tiwa
def: "A group of related Tanoan Puebloans in New Mexico. They traditionally spoke a Tiwa language (although some speakers have switched to Spanish and/or English), and are divided into the two Northern Tiwa groups, in Taos and Picuris, and the Southern Tiwa in Isleta and Sandia, around what is now Albuquerque, and in Ysleta del Sur near El Paso, Texas." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Tiwa
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiwa_Puebloans
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1639219
is_a: GSSO:005935 ! Tanoan

[Term]
id: GSSO:005937
name: Tewa
def: "A linguistic group of Pueblo Native Americans who speak the Tewa language and share the Pueblo culture. Their homelands are on or near the Rio Grande in New Mexico north of Santa Fe." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Tewa
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tewa
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1974818
is_a: GSSO:005935 ! Tanoan

[Term]
id: GSSO:005938
name: Northern Tiwa
def: "Any of various Indigenous Tiwa peoples who speak Northern Tiwa languages, primarily Taos and Picuris." []
is_a: GSSO:005936 ! Tiwa

[Term]
id: GSSO:005939
name: Southern Tiwa
def: "Any of various Indigenous Tiwa peoples who speak Northern Tiwa languages, primarily Sandia, Isleta, and Ysleta del Sur (Tigua)." []
synonym: "Isleta Tiwa" NARROW []
is_a: GSSO:005936 ! Tiwa

[Term]
id: GSSO:005940
name: Takelma
def: "A Native American people who originally lived in the Rogue Valley of interior southwestern Oregon. Most of their villages were sited along the Rogue River. The name Takelma means \"(Those) Along the River\"." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Takelma
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Takelma
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2508529
is_a: GSSO:001027 ! North American ethnic group

[Term]
id: GSSO:005941
name: Shoshone
def: "A Native American tribe with four large cultural/linguistic divisions, those being the Eastern, Northern, and Western Shoshone, together with the Gosiute." []
