[Term]
id: GSSO:005942
name: Western Shoshone
def: "Any of several Shoshone tribes that are Indigenous to the Great Basin and have lands identified in the Treaty of Ruby Valley 1863. They resided in Idaho, Nevada, California, and Utah. The tribes are very closely related culturally to the Paiute, Goshute, Bannock, Ute, and Timbisha tribes. They speak the Western dialect of the Shoshone language." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Shoshone
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2565472
is_a: GSSO:005941 ! Shoshone

[Term]
id: GSSO:005943
name: Goshute
def: "A tribe of Western Shoshone Native Americans." []
