[Term]
id: GSSO:005944
name: Northern Shoshone
def: "Shoshone of the Snake River Plain of southern Idaho and the northeast of the Great Basin where Idaho, Wyoming and Utah meet. They are culturally affiliated with the Bannock people and are in the Great Basin classification of Indigenous People." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Shoshone
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2006743
is_a: GSSO:005941 ! Shoshone

[Term]
id: GSSO:005945
name: Bannock
def: "Originally Northern Paiute but are more culturally affiliated with the Northern Shoshone. They are in the Great Basin classification of Indigenous People. Their traditional lands include northern Nevada, southeastern Oregon, southern Idaho, and western Wyoming. Today they are enrolled in the federally recognized Shoshone-Bannock Tribes of the Fort Hall Reservation of Idaho, located on the Fort Hall Indian Reservation." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bannock_people
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Bannock
