[Term]
id: GSSO:005958
name: Kaw
def: "A federally recognized Native American tribe in Oklahoma and parts of Kansas. They come from the central Midwestern United States. The tribe known as Kaw have also been known as the \"People of the South wind\", \"People of water\", Kansa, Kaza, Kosa, and Kasa. Their tribal language is Kansa, classified as a Siouan language." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaw_people
