[Term]
id: GSSO:005978
name: Laguna Pueblo
def: "A federally recognized tribe of Native American Pueblo people in west-central New Mexico, USA. The name, Laguna, is Spanish (meaning \"small lake\") and derives from the lake located on their reservation. This body of water was formed by an ancient dam that was constructed by the Laguna people." []
