[Term]
id: GSSO:005982
name: Acjachemen
def: "An Indigenous people of California. They traditionally lived along the coast in what is now Orange and San Diego counties." []
comment: Acjachemen were referred to as Juaneño by Spanish colonizers following baptism at Mission San Juan Capistrano in the late eighteenth century. Today many contemporary members of the tribe who identify as descendants of the Indigenous society living in the local San Juan and San Mateo Creek drainage areas prefer the term Acjachemen as their autonym, or name for themselves, in an effort to decolonize their history.
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acjachemen
