[Term]
id: GSSO:005990
name: Salish
def: "An ethno-linguistic group of the Pacific Northwest, identified by their use of the Salish languages which diversified out of Proto-Salish between 3,000 and 6,000 years ago." []
comment: The term “Salish” originated in the modern era as an exonym created for linguistic research. Salish is an Anglicization of Séliš, the endonym for the Salish Tribes of the Flathead Reservation.
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salish_peoples
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1825812
is_a: GSSO:001027 ! North American ethnic group

[Term]
id: GSSO:005991
name: Coast Salish
def: "A group of ethnically and linguistically related Indigenous peoples of the Pacific Northwest Coast, living in British Columbia, Canada and the U.S. states of Washington and Oregon. They speak one of the Coast Salish languages. Nuxalk (Bella Coola) nation are usually included in the group, although their language is more closely related to Interior Salish languages." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Coast_Salish
