[Term]
id: GSSO:006001
name: Crow
def: "Native Americans living primarily in southern Montana. Today, the Crow people have a federally recognized tribe, the Crow Tribe of Montana, with an Indian reservation located in the south-central part of the state. The Crow are a Plains tribe, who speak the Crow language, part of the Missouri River Valley branch of Siouan languages." []
