[Term]
id: GSSO:006003
name: Cocopah
def: "Native Americans who live in Baja California and Sonora, Mexico, and in Arizona in the United States. They speak the Cocopah language, which belongs to the Delta–California branch of the Yuman family. The Spanish term for Cocopah is Cucapá." []
