[Term]
id: GSSO:006234
name: medicalization
def: "A process by which nonmedical problems become defined and treated as medical problems, usually in terms of illnesses, or disorders." []
def: "The process by which human conditions and problems come to be defined and treated as medical conditions, and thus become the subject of medical study, diagnosis, prevention, or treatment. Medicalization can be driven by new evidence or hypotheses about conditions; by changing social attitudes or economic considerations; or by the development of new medications or treatments." []
synonym: "disease mongering" RELATED [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disease_mongering, https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1228633] {def="A term for the practice of widening the diagnostic boundaries of illnesses and aggressively promoting their public awareness in order to expand the markets for treatment. Among the entities benefiting from selling and delivering treatments are pharmaceutical companies, physicians, alternative practitioners and other professional or consumer organizations. It is distinct from the promulgation of bogus or unrecognised diagnoses."}
synonym: "pathologization" RELATED []
synonym: "patologisering" RELATED [https://lgbt.dk/ordbog/patologisering/]
is_a: GSSO:006233 ! medical process
property_value: dc:identifier "https://homosaurus.org/terms/medicalisation" xsd:anyURI {terms:source="http://web.archive.org/web/20160404165237/https://homosaurus.org/terms"}
