[Term]
id: GSSO:006271
name: 5α-reductase inhibitor
def: "Any substance that inhibits steroid 5-alpha-reductase, an enzyme that converts testosterone into dihydrotestosterone (DHT). Since DHT has three times greater affinity for androgen receptors than testosterone, inhibition of 5-alpha-reductase results in a strong reduction in the androgenic effects of testosterone." []
