[Term]
id: GSSO:006407
name: date rape drug
def: "Any drug that incapacitates another person and renders them vulnerable to a sexual assault, including rape. The substances are associated with date rape because of reported incidents of their use in the context of two people dating, during which the victim is sexually assaulted or raped, or suffers other indignities. The substances are not exclusively used to perpetrate sexual assault or rape, but are the properties or side-effects of substances normally used for legitimate medical purposes. One of the most common incapacitating agents for date rape is alcohol, administered either surreptitiously or consumed voluntarily, rendering the victim unable to make informed decisions or give consent." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Date_rape_drug
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q899702
is_a: SIO:010038 ! drug
property_value: schema:alternateName "date rape drugs" xsd:string

