[Term]
id: GSSO:006632
name: writing
def: "A medium of human communication that represents language with signs and symbols. For languages that utilize a writing system, inscriptions can complement spoken language by creating a durable version of speech that can be stored for future reference or transmitted across distance. Writing, in other words, is not a language, but a tool used to make languages readable. Within a language system, writing relies on many of the same structures as speech, such as vocabulary, grammar, and semantics, with the added dependency of a system of signs or symbols." []
synonym: "written language" RELATED [] {schema:alternateName="written languages"}
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Writing
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Writing
