property_value: Property:P3095 GSSO:005774

[Term]
id: GSSO:006633
name: inclusive writing
def: "Inclusive writing is writing which utilizes \"people-first language\", or language that makes personhood the essential characteristic of any described person, and self-identification, i.e. striving to include language which is self-conscious and respects peoples' choices in relation to their identities. At its core inclusive writing should not avoid stereotypes and other prejudices, while emphasizing the language preferred by that person, people, community, or group." []
comment: As an example, using "people of color" instead of "minorities" or "transgender person" instead of "transgendered".
comment: It is important than inclusive writing should not be erasing of historical mistreatment.
is_a: GSSO:006632 ! writing

[Term]
id: GSSO:006634
name: gender-inclusive writing
def: "Generally, practices which encourage and normalize non-sexist language and gender expansiveness (such as providing pronouns in resumes, websites, etc.; providing places to add preferred names; avoiding language which excludes other genders; etc.)." []
comment: Some examples would be using "firefighter" instead of "fireman", "flight attendant" instead of "stewardess", or "congressperson" instead of "congressman".
is_a: GSSO:006633 ! inclusive writing

