[Term]
id: GSSO:006668
name: abuse defense
def: "A criminal law defense in which the defendant argues that a prior history of abuse justifies violent retaliation. While the term most often refers to instances of child abuse or sexual assault, it also refers more generally to any attempt by the defense to use a syndrome or societal condition to deflect responsibility away from the defendant." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abuse_defense
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4670673
is_a: GSSO:003542 ! panic defense
property_value: schema:alternateName "abuse defenses" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:006669
name: infancy defense
def: "A form of defense known as an excuse so that defendants falling within the definition of an \"infant\" are excluded from criminal liability for their actions, if at the relevant time, they had not reached an age of criminal responsibility. After reaching the initial age, there may be levels of responsibility dictated by age and the type of offense committed." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Defense_of_infancy
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q129218
is_a: GSSO:003539 ! excuse defense
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "defense of infancy" xsd:string
property_value: schema:alternateName "infancy defenses" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:006670
name: automatism defense
def: "A rarely used criminal defense. It is one of the mental condition defenses that relate to the mental state of the defendant. Automatism can be seen variously as lack of voluntariness, lack of culpability (unconsciousness) or excuse (Schopp). Automatism means that the defendant was not aware of his or her actions when making the particular movements that constituted the illegal act." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automatism_(law)
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4826641
is_a: GSSO:003539 ! excuse defense
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "automatism" xsd:string
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "defense of automatism" xsd:string

