[Term]
id: GSSO:006677
name: mistake of fact defense
def: "A mistake of fact may sometimes mean that, while a person has committed the physical element of an offence, because they were labouring under a mistake of fact, they never formed the required mens rea, and so will escape liability for offences that require mens rea." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mistake_(criminal_law)
