[Term]
id: GSSO:006678
name: provocation defense
def: "In law, provocation is when a person is considered to have committed a criminal act partly because of a preceding set of events that might cause a reasonable person to lose self control. This makes them less morally culpable than if the act was premeditated (pre-planned) and done out of pure malice (malice aforethought)." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Provocation_(legal)
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3566104
is_a: GSSO:006675 ! exculpatory defense

