[Term]
id: GSSO:006753
name: enthusiastic consent
def: "A variant of \"yes means yes\" consent is enthusiastic consent. Project Respect states that \"positive sexuality\" needs to start with enthusiastic consent\" in which a person is as \"excited and into someone else’s enjoyment\" a they are, an engaged partner. Planned Parenthood says that enthusiastic consent can be seen when a partner is \"...happy, excited, or energized\"." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sexual_consent#Enthusiastic_consent
is_a: GSSO:006758 ! affirmative consent

[Term]
id: GSSO:006754
name: expressed consent
def: "Consent expressed specifically, either verbally or in the form of writing." []
is_a: NCIT:C25460 ! samtykke

[Term]
id: GSSO:006755
name: implied consent
def: "Consent which is not expressly granted by a person, but rather implicitly granted by a person's actions and the facts and circumstances of a particular situation (or in some cases, by a person's silence or inaction). The term is most commonly encountered in the context of United States drunk driving laws. There are no U.S. states that allow implied consent as an excuse for rape in a court of law." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Implied_consent
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q6007337
is_a: NCIT:C25460 ! samtykke

[Term]
id: GSSO:006757
name: presumed consent
def: "An institutional policy of granting authority to health personnel to perform procedures on patients or to remove organs from cadavers for transplantation unless an objection is registered by family members or by the patient prior to death. This also includes emergency care of minors without prior parental consent." []
is_a: NCIT:C25460 ! samtykke
property_value: Property:P486 "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D019724" xsd:anyURI

