[Term]
id: GSSO:006905
name: binge-eating disorder
def: "A disorder associated with three or more of the following: eating until feeling uncomfortably full; eating large amounts of food when not physically hungry; eating much more rapidly than normal; eating alone due to embarrassment; feeling of disgust, depression, or guilt after overeating. Criteria includes occurrence on average, at least 2 days a week for 6 months. The binge eating is not associated with the regular use of inappropriate compensatory behavior (i.e. purging, excessive exercise, etc.) and does not co-occur exclusively with bulimia nervosa or anorexia nervosa." []
synonym: "binge eating disorder" EXACT [] {schema:alternateName="binge eating disorders"}
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binge_eating_disorder
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q209522
