[Term]
id: GSSO:006968
name: Denys-Drash syndrome
def: "An autosomal dominant disease that is characterized by the association of diffuse mesangial sclerosis (DMS), intersex anatomy with a 46,XY karyotype, and nephroblastoma that derives from an abnormality in the WT1 gene (Wilms' tumor suppressor gene)." []
synonym: "Denys Drash syndrome" EXACT []
