[Term]
id: GSSO:007072
name: uniparental disomy
def: "The presence in a cell of two paired chromosomes from the same parent, with no chromosome of that pair from the other parent. This chromosome composition stems from non-disjunction events during meiosis. The disomy may be composed of both homologous chromosomes from one parent (heterodisomy) or a duplicate of one chromosome (isodisomy)." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uniparental_disomy
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1207929
