[Term]
id: GSSO:007232
name: ethnic identity
def: "An ethnic identity is the identification with a certain ethnicity, usually on the basis of a presumed common genealogy or ancestry. Recognition by others as a distinct ethnic group is often a contributing factor to developing this bond of identification. Ethnic groups are also often united by common cultural, behavioral, linguistic, ritualistic, or religious traits." []
synonym: "racial and ethnic identity" BROAD [] {terms:isReferencedBy="http://web.archive.org/web/20210619072006/https://epi.washington.edu/sites/default/files/website_documents/DEI%20Glossary_Formatted_20190711.pdf"}
