[Term]
id: GSSO:007395
name: genderswap
def: "A trope in fanfiction (and especially in fanart) which involves characters \"swapping\" gender, typically male-to-female or female-to-male. The idea that every fictional character has a genderswapped counterpart is referred to as Rule 63." []
def: "An instance of changing a fictional character's biological sex and/or gender identity from the canonical norm." []
comment: "Genderbend" is sometimes used as a synonym for genderswap, but the two are explicitly differentiated in order to avoid confusion, with one (swapping) referring to fictional characters changing gender, whereas the other (bending) refers to "bending" of expected gender roles in any context, including in real life (sometimes as a form of social activism).
synonym: "genderswapping" RELATED [] {EXACT="gender swapping"}
xref: https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/genderswap
is_a: GSSO:003556 ! brouillage des genres
property_value: dc:identifier "http://homosaurus.org/v2/genderSwapping" xsd:anyURI {terms:source="https://web.archive.org/web/20190828104105/http://homosaurus.org/v2"}
property_value: Property:P5191 NCIT:C17357
property_value: seeAlso GSSO:008789

[Term]
id: GSSO:007398
name: Two-Spirit gender identity
def: "A Native (North) American who is non-cisgender, non-binary or gender-variant (especially one belonging to a traditional tribal third-gender, fourth-gender or transgender category)." []
def: "Two-Spirit is a modern, pan-Indian, umbrella term used by some Indigenous North Americans to describe certain people in their communities who fulfill a traditional third-gender (or other gender non-conforming) ceremonial role in their cultures." []
comment: Depending on context, Two-Spirit may refer to a gender identity and/or role, a sexual orientation and/or sexuality, both, or neither. This entry is intended to represent cases which context refers to gender identity. Use more specific entries where applicable.
comment: Note that some Indigenous Australians and Torres Strait Islanders use the term "Two-Spirit" as a gender identity as well, but in somewhat different contexts.
comment: Note that the term Two-Spirit is sometimes used as an umbrella term for Native American and First Nation culturally-specific gender and sexual roles, outside of Eurocentric and colonialist frameworks. However, it is more appropriate to use the specific identity a Native American or First Nation person uses (or used in life), especially if it is tribe specific. Many persons falling under these roles actively do not consider themselves to be Two-Spirit.
comment: The term "Two Spirit" was adopted by consensus in 1990 at an international gay and lesbian Indigenous gathering as a replacement for the inappropriate and outdated term "berdache".
