[Term]
id: GSSO:007596
name: cultural pluralism
def: "A term used when smaller groups within a larger society maintain their unique cultural identities, and their values and practices are accepted by the wider dominant culture provided they are consistent with the laws and values of the wider society." []
synonym: "multi-culturalism" RELATED []
synonym: "multi-culturism" RELATED []
