[Term]
id: GSSO:007818
name: street dance
def: "A dance style that evolved outside dance studios in any available open space such as streets, dance parties, block parties, parks, school yards, raves, and nightclubs." []
synonym: "street dancing" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Street_dance
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Street_dance
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1061584
is_a: GSSO:007819 ! vernacular dance
property_value: schema:alternateName "street dances" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:007819
name: vernacular dance
def: "Dances which have developed \"naturally\" as a part of \"everyday\" culture within a particular community. In contrast to the elite and official culture, vernacular dances are usually learned naturally without formal instruction.." []
synonym: "vernacular dancing" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vernacular_dance
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q22909628
is_a: GSSO:004299 ! dance
property_value: schema:alternateName "vernacular dances" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:007820
name: house dance
def: "A social dance and street dance primarily danced to house music, that has roots in the clubs of Chicago and of New York. The main elements of house dance include footwork, jacking, and lofting. House dance is often improvised and emphasizes fast and complex foot-oriented steps combined with fluid movements in the torso, as well as floor work." []
synonym: "house dancing" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_dance
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4356517
is_a: GSSO:007818 ! street dance
property_value: schema:alternateName "house dances" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:007821
name: vogue
def: "A highly stylized, modern house dance originating in the late 1980s that evolved out of the Harlem ballroom scene of the 1960s. It gained mainstream exposure when it was featured in Madonna's song and video \"Vogue\" (1990), and when showcased in the 1990 documentary Paris Is Burning (which went on to win the Grand Jury Prize at the 1991 Sundance Film Festival)." []
synonym: "vogueing" RELATED []
synonym: "voguing" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vogue_(dance)
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1112128
is_a: GSSO:007820 ! house dance
