[Term]
id: GSSO:007829
name: Skoptsy
name: скопцы
def: "A sect within the larger Spiritual Christianity movement in the Russian Empire, best known for practicing castration of men and the mastectomy of women in accordance with their teachings against sexual lust. The movement emerged in the late 18th century. It reached the peak of its popularity in the early 20th century, with as many as 100,000 members, in spite of persecution by the imperial government." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skoptsy
