[Term]
id: GSSO:007854
name: kteuy
name: ខ្ទើយ
def: "A Khmer term for a culturally specific gender identity considered intermediate between pros (ប្រុស, male) and srey (ស្រី, female)." []
comment: The broad category of kteuy covers two distinct sub-groupings, "short hairs" and "long hairs". Short hairs (សក់​ខ្លី, sak klay) are men who dress and identify as men but have sex with "real" men; they are usually married, and very few of them have sex exclusively with men. Long hairs (សក់​វែង, sak veng, also called ស្រីស្រស់, srey sros, "charming girls"), identify and behave as women, and may use hormones and surgery to feminize their appearance. They call themselves kteuy, but may feel insulted if outsiders use this term.
synonym: "GSSO:002306" RELATED []
is_a: GSSO:002024 ! gendered person
is_a: GSSO:011266 ! Southeast Asian culturally-specific gender identity
property_value: schema:alternateName "kteuys" xsd:string
property_value: schema:identifier "http://homosaurus.org/v2/kteuy" xsd:anyURI {terms:source="https://web.archive.org/web/20190828104105/http://homosaurus.org/v2"}
property_value: terms:isReferencedBy https://books.google.com/books?id=hi8lDwAAQBAJ

[Term]
id: GSSO:007855
name: sak klay
name: សក់​ខ្
def: "A term in Khmer used to refer to a man who acts and dresses stereotypically masculine and engages in sexual activities with other men, but is typically married to a woman and does not usually exclusively have sex with men." []
is_a: GSSO:007854 ! kteuy
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "short hairs" xsd:string
property_value: terms:isReferencedBy https://books.google.com/books?id=hi8lDwAAQBAJ

[Term]
id: GSSO:007856
