[Term]
id: GSSO:007859
name: calabai
def: "One of five gender categories observed in Bugis culture. A calabai is a person typically assigned male at birth who takes on a more feminine role. Such persons live as women in this sense, but do not think of themselves as female and are thought of as male by other men." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gender_in_Bugis_society#Calabai
