[Term]
id: GSSO:007860
name: calalai
def: "One of five gender categories observed in Bugis culture. A calalai is a person typically assigned female at birth who takes on a more masculine role. Such persons dress and present as men, hold stereotypically masculine professions, and usually live with female partners to adopt children." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gender_in_Bugis_society#Calalai
