[Term]
id: GSSO:008112
name: Corded Ware culture
def: "An archaeological culture comprising a broad archaeological horizon of Europe between c. 2900 BCE – c. 2350 BCE, thus from the late Neolithic, through the Copper Age, and ending in the early Bronze Age. Corded Ware culture encompassed a vast area, from the Rhine on the west to the Volga in the east, occupying parts of Northern Europe, Central Europe and Eastern Europe." []
