[Term]
id: GSSO:008131
name: palliative care
def: "An interdisciplinary medical caregiving approach aimed at optimizing quality of life and mitigating suffering among people with serious, complex illness. Within the published literature, many definitions of palliative care exist; most notably, the World Health Organization describes palliative care as \"an approach that improves the quality of life of patients and their families facing the problems associated with life-threatening illness, through the prevention and relief of suffering by means of early identification and impeccable assessment and treatment of pain and other problems, physical, psychosocial, and spiritual.”" []
synonym: "encounter for palliative care" RELATED [] {Property:P4229="Z51.5", Property:P1692="V66.7"}
