[Term]
id: GSSO:008182
name: passive immunity
def: "The transfer of active humoral immunity of ready-made antibodies. Passive immunity can occur naturally, when maternal antibodies are transferred to the fetus through the placenta, and it can also be induced artificially, when high levels of antibodies specific to a pathogen or toxin (obtained from humans, horses, or other animals) are transferred to non-immune persons through blood products that contain antibodies, such as in immunoglobulin therapy or antiserum therapy." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Passive_immunity
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q382646
is_a: NCIT:C16710 ! immunity

