[Term]
id: GSSO:008218
name: Independent Catholicism
def: "A denominational movement of clergy and laity who self-identify as Catholic (most often as Old Catholic and/or as Independent Catholic) and form \"micro-churches claiming apostolic succession and valid sacraments\"." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Independent_Catholicism
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independent_Catholicism
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q159108
is_a: GSSO:007371 ! Catholicism

[Term]
id: GSSO:008219
name: Old Catholicism
def: "A term used from the 1850s by groups which had separated from the Roman Catholic Church over certain doctrines, primarily concerned with papal authority; some of these groups, especially in the Netherlands, had already existed long before the term. These churches are not in full communion with the Holy See. Member churches of the Union of Utrecht of the Old Catholic Churches (UU) are in full communion with the Anglican Communion, and some are members of the World Council of Churches." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Old_Catholicism
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Catholic_Church
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5169816
