[Term]
id: GSSO:008252
name: slash fiction
def: "A genre of fan fiction that focuses on romantic or sexual relationships between fictional characters of the same sex. While the term \"slash\" originally only referred to stories where male characters were involved in an explicit sexual relationship as a primary plot element (also known as \"m/m slash\"), it is now used to refer to any fan story containing a pairing between same-sex characters. Many fans distinguish female-focused slash as a separate genre, commonly referred to as femslash (also known as \"f/f slash\" or \"femmeslash\")." []
synonym: "m/m" NARROW []
synonym: "m/m slash" NARROW []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Slash_fiction
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slash_fiction
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1075191
is_a: GSSO:008829 ! LGBTQ fan fiction
is_a: GSSO:008840 ! slash media
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "slash fan fiction" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:008253
name: femslash
def: "A subgenre of slash fan fiction which focuses on romantic and/or sexual relationships between female fictional characters. Typically, characters featured in femslash are heterosexual in the canon universe; however, similar fan fiction about lesbian or bisexual female characters is commonly labeled as femslash for convenience." []
synonym: "girlslash" NARROW []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Femslash
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5442941
is_a: GSSO:008252 ! slash fiction
