[Term]
id: GSSO:008284
name: Indigenous person of Canada
def: "A person belonging to any of various Indigenous peoples within the boundaries of Canada. They comprise the First Nations, Inuit, and Métis. Although \"Indian\" is a term still commonly used in legal documents, the descriptors \"Indian\" and \"Eskimo\" have somewhat fallen into disuse in Canada and some consider them to be pejorative." []
