[Term]
id: GSSO:008289
name: Melanesian
def: "The predominant and Indigenous inhabitants of Melanesia, in a wide area from Maluku Islands and New Guinea to as far east as the islands of Vanuatu and Fiji. Most speak either one of the many languages of the Austronesian language family, especially ones in the Oceanic branch, or from one of the many unrelated families of Papuan languages." []
synonym: "GSSO:008292" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Melanesian_people
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melanesians
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1762752
is_a: GSSO:001026 ! Oceanic ethnic group
property_value: Property:P276 GAZ:00005860
property_value: schema:alternateName "Melanesians" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:008290
name: Papuan
def: "An Indigenous person of New Guinea belonging to one of two major historical lineages: (1) a first wave from the Malay archipelago perhaps 50,000 years ago when New Guinea and Australia were a single landmass called Sahul, and (2) much later a wave of Austronesian people from the north who introduced Austronesian languages and pigs about 3,500 years ago, and who left a small but significant genetic trace in many coastal Papuan peoples (though only a minority of Austronesian-speaking Papuans have detectable Austronesian ancestry)." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Papuan_people
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_people_of_New_Guinea
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q424129
