[Term]
id: GSSO:008981
name: race-reversed casting
def: "A form of nontraditional casting in acting which revolves around reversing the race of characters being played (white characters being played by Black actors and vice versa). The concept was intended as a way to open up non-traditional character roles to more actors but has received complaints that it waters down racial differences." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Race-reversed_casting
