[Term]
id: GSSO:009006
name: survivor syndrome
def: "A term used to describe the reactions and behaviors of people who have survived massive and adverse events, such as the Holocaust, the Rape of Nanking, and the HIV/AIDS epidemic." []
comment: When the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders IV (DSM-IV) was published, survivor guilt was removed as a recognized specific diagnosis, and redefined as a significant symptom of post-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD).
synonym: "concentration camp syndrome" NARROW [] {hasSynonym="KZ syndrome"}
is_a: GSSO:000517 ! psychiatric syndrome
