[Term]
id: GSSO:009012
name: biological determinism
def: "The belief that human behavior is directly controlled by an individual's genes or some component of their physiology, generally at the expense of the role of the environment, whether in embryonic development or in learning." []
synonym: "genetic determinism" NARROW [] {def="The theory that human character and behavior are shaped by the genes that comprise the individual's genotype rather than by culture; environment; and individual choice.", Property:P486="http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D033141"}
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biological_determinism
