[Term]
id: GSSO:009046
name: racialization
def: "The process of ascribing ethnic or racial identities to a relationship, social practice, or group that did not identify itself as such. Racialization or ethnicization often arises out of the interaction of a group with a group that it dominates and ascribes a racial identity to for the purpose of continued domination. While this ascribed identity is often born out of domination, the racialized and ethnicized group often gradually identifies with and even embraces this identity and thus becomes a self-ascribed race or ethnicity. These processes have been common throughout the history of imperialism, nationalism, and racial and ethnic hierarchies." []
synonym: "ethnicization" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Racialization
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q10649809
is_a: GSSO:003653 ! domination
property_value: Property:P5191 GSSO:002199
property_value: terms:isReferencedBy GSSO:011100
property_value: terms:isReferencedBy http://web.archive.org/web/20200721053627/https://sacred.omeka.net/glossary
property_value: terms:isReferencedBy http://web.archive.org/web/20220131044449/https://www.ama-assn.org/system/files/ama-aamc-equity-guide.pdf

