[Term]
id: GSSO:009285
name: hybridity theory
def: "A postcolonial theory which reevaluates the assumption of colonial identity through the repetition of discriminatory identity effects. In this way, hybridity can unsettle the narcissist demands of colonial power, but reforms its identifications in strategies of subversion that turn the gaze of the discriminated back upon the colonist." []
synonym: "hybridism" RELATED []
synonym: "hybridity" RELATED []
is_a: GSSO:009279 ! postcolonial theory
