[Term]
id: GSSO:009349
name: Baroque music
def: "A period or style of Western art music composed from approximately 1600 to 1750. This era followed the Renaissance music era, and was followed in turn by the Classical era, with the galant style marking the transition between Baroque and Classical eras. The Baroque period is divided into three major phases: early, middle, and late. Overlapping in time, they are conventionally dated from 1580 to 1650, from 1630 to 1700, and from 1680 to 1750." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baroque_music
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Baroque_music
