[Term]
id: GSSO:009418
name: assigned gender at birth
name: genre assigné à la naissance {terms:isReferencedBy="GSSO:011927"}
def: "Assigned gender is one's gender which was assigned at birth, typically by a medical and/or legal organization, and then later registered with other organizations. Such a designation is typically based off of the superficial appearance of external genitalia present at birth." []
comment: Asking for assigned gender at birth may not be necessary depending on context; an organ inventory may be more useful in health care.
comment: Note that this is not always based off of the original birth certificate depending on the jurisdiction. It may also be illegal to ask for this information as well.
