[Term]
id: GSSO:009454
name: nightcore
def: "A genre of music in which a cover track is sped up from its source material by 10-30%. The name is derived from Nightcore, a Norwegian duo who released pitch-shifted versions of trance and eurodance songs, but now more broadly refers to any sped-up cover. Nightcore is also commonly associated with anime, with many YouTube thumbnails of nightcore remixes containing anime characters and art." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nightcore
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3876770
is_a: GSSO:009453 ! remixed electronic music

