property_value: Property:P1535 GSSO:009500
property_value: Property:P1813 "cabaret" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:009503
name: American burlesque
def: "A theatrical genre derived from elements of Victorian burlesque, music hall and minstrel shows. Burlesque in America became popular in the late 1860s and slowly evolved to feature ribald comedy and female nudity. By the early 1930s the striptease element of burlesque overshadowed the comedy and subjected burlesque to extensive local legislation. Burlesque gradually lost popularity beginning in the 1940s. A number of producers sought to capitalize on nostalgia for the entertainment by attempting to recreate the spirit of burlesque in Hollywood films from the 1930s to the 1960s. There has been a resurgence of interest in this format since the 1990s." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_burlesque
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4745432
is_a: GSSO:009501 ! burlesque theatre

[Term]
id: GSSO:009504
name: Neo-Burlesque
def: "The revival and updating of the traditional American burlesque performance. Though based on the traditional burlesque art, the new form encompasses a wider range of performance styles; neo-burlesque acts can range from anything from classic striptease to modern dance to theatrical mini-dramas to comedic mayhem." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neo-Burlesque
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1982463
is_a: GSSO:009501 ! burlesque theatre
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "New Burlesque" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:009505
name: boylesque
def: "Neo-burlesque shows that feature male-body roles have been dubbed as boylesque. The introduction of boylesque elements can be seen as a key difference between neo-burlesque and earlier, exclusively female-body forms of burlesque, which sometimes incorporated drag-queen roles (i.e. male impersonators of female bodies) but did not directly represent masculinity. Boylesque within the neo-burlesque scene can be traced back to the early 1980s with performers like John Sex." []
is_a: GSSO:009504 ! Neo-Burlesque

