[Term]
id: GSSO:009682
name: Ancient Greek religion
def: "The collection of beliefs, rituals, and mythology originating in ancient Greece in the form of both popular public religion and cult practices. These groups varied enough for it to be possible to speak of Greek religions or \"cults\" in the plural, though most of them shared similarities." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Greek_religion
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Ancient_Greek_religion
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q855270
