[Term]
id: GSSO:009759
name: preemptive abortion
def: "Use of an abortifacient to prevent embryonic implantation in the event that fertilization has occurred. Various methods are used to do this: the morning-after pill (diethylstilbesterol), prostaglandins in vaginal suppositories, and RU 486 (mifepristone). Menstrual extraction was also somewhat popular in the 1970s, but is no longer recommended." []
