[Term]
id: GSSO:009822
name: developmental-descriptive profile
def: "A profile proposed by William Prendergast in 1979 to describe possible psychological outcomes for children with \"inadequate\" personalities. Prendergast's model is now largely considered pseudoscientific." []
is_a: GSSO:009821 ! psychological profile
property_value: schema:alternateName "developmental-descriptive profiles" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:009823
name: acceptor developmental-descriptive profile
def: "A personality profile originating from the mostly obsoleted 1979 William Prendergast developmental-descriptive profile. The profile involves an individual's attempt to cope with their social \"inadequacy\" via seduction, leading to antisocial behavior. The combination of such a personality with unresolved early sexual trauma was said to lead to a person becoming a \"seductive pedophile, a seduction-motivated exhibitionist, a passive homosexual, voyeur, sexually motivated arsonist, or obscene phone caller with seduction fantasies\"." []
is_a: GSSO:009822 ! developmental-descriptive profile
property_value: Property:P1813 "acceptor" xsd:string
property_value: terms:isReferencedBy https://books.google.com/books/?id=ymkYAAAAIAAJ

