[Term]
id: GSSO:009830
name: right to internet access
def: "The right which stipulates all people must be able to access the internet in order to exercise and enjoy their rights to freedom of expression and opinion and other fundamental human rights, that states have a responsibility to ensure that internet access is broadly available, and that states may not unreasonably restrict an individual's access to the internet." []
