[Term]
id: GSSO:009840
name: Kingdom of Ndongo
def: "An early-modern African state located in what is now Angola. The Kingdom of Ndongo is first recorded in the sixteenth century. It was one of multiple vassal states to Kongo, though Ndongo was the most powerful of these with a king called the Ngola. Little is known of the kingdom in the early sixteenth century. \"Angola\" was listed among the titles of the King of Kongo in 1535, so it is likely that it was in somewhat subordinate to Kongo. Its own oral traditions, collected in the late sixteenth century, particularly by the Jesuit Baltasar Barreira, described the founder of the kingdom, Ngola Kiluanje, also known as Ngola Inene, as a migrant from Kongo, chief of a Kimbundu-speaking ethnic group." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Ndongo
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1796232
is_a: http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D017516 ! historical geographic location

[Term]
id: GSSO:009841
name: psychological accommodation
def: "A process which is part of Jean Piaget's theory of psychological adaptation (psychological adjustment). It describes the process by which individuals' congitive schemas and perceptions adapt to situations which cause conflict with those schemas or perceptions, without necessarily resolving the basis of conflict or changing the underlying system which causes the conflict." []
is_a: GSSO:003648 ! psychological adjustment
