[Term]
id: GSSO:009937
name: Aztec religion
def: "A religion which originated among the Aztecs in central Mexico. Like other Mesoamerican religions, it also has practices such as human sacrifice in connection with many religious festivals which are in the Aztec calendar. This polytheistic religion has many gods and goddesses; the Aztecs would often incorporate deities that were borrowed from other geographic regions and peoples into their own religious practices." []
synonym: "Aztec mythology and religion" BROAD [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Aztec_mythology_and_religion]
