[Term]
id: GSSO:009940
name: supercontinent
def: "The assembly of most or all of Earth's continental blocks or cratons to form a single large landmass. However, some earth scientists use a different definition: \"a grouping of formerly dispersed continents\", which leaves room for interpretation and is easier to apply to Precambrian times, although a minimum of about 75% of the continental crust then in existence has been proposed as a limit to separate supercontinents from other groupings." []
