[Term]
id: GSSO:009942
name: mediterranean sea
def: "A mostly enclosed sea that has limited exchange of water with outer oceans and with water circulation dominated by salinity and temperature differences rather than winds or tides." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mediterranean_sea_(oceanography)
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q986177
is_a: GSSO:009941 ! marginal sea
property_value: schema:alternateName "mediterranean seas" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:009943
name: concentration basin
def: "A mediterranean sea with higher salinity than the outer ocean due to evaporation, and water exchange consisting of inflow of the fresher oceanic water in the upper layer and outflow of the saltier mediterranean water in the lower layer of the connecting channel." []
is_a: GSSO:009942 ! mediterranean sea
property_value: schema:alternateName "concentration basins" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:009944
name: dilution basin
def: "A mediterranean sea with lower salinity due to freshwater gains such as rainfall and rivers, and water exchange consisting of outflow of the fresher mediterranean water in the upper layer and inflow of the saltier oceanic water in the lower layer of the channel. Renewal of deep water may not be sufficient to supply oxygen to the bottom." []
is_a: GSSO:009942 ! mediterranean sea
property_value: schema:alternateName "dilution basins" xsd:string

