[Term]
id: GSSO:009971
name: reproductive coercion
def: "Any of a collection of behaviors that interfere with decision-making related to reproductive health. These behaviors are meant to maintain power and control related to reproductive health by a current, former, or hopeful intimate or romantic partner, but they can also be perpetrated by parents or in-laws. Ultimately, these behaviors infringe on individuals' reproductive rights and reduce their reproductive autonomy." []
synonym: "reproductive control" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reproductive_coercion
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7314307
is_a: GSSO:009970 ! coercion
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "coerced reproduction" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:009972
name: pregnancy coercion
comment: A type of reproductive coercion which includes any behaviors intended to coerce or pressure a partner to become or not become pregnant. Pregnancy coercion involves various tactics, including verbal threats related to impregnation, coerced sex, refusal to use male-controlled contraception (i.e., condoms, withdrawal), interference with or pressure not to use female controlled contraception (i.e., hormonal methods), monitoring menstrual cycles or gynecological visits, pressure for or against sterilization, and monitoring of ovulation.
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reproductive_coercion#Pregnancy_coercion
is_a: GSSO:009971 ! reproductive coercion

[Term]
id: GSSO:009973
name: forced abortion
def: "An induced abortion which occurs when a perpetrator or perpetrators cause abortion by force, threat or coercion, or by taking advantage of a person's incapability to give consent, or where they provide them consent under duress." []
synonym: "coerced abortion" RELATED [] {schema:alternateName="coerced abortions"}
synonym: "compulsory abortion" RELATED [] {schema:alternateName="compulsory abortions"}
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Forced_abortion
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forced_abortion
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q231577
is_a: GSSO:004414 ! induced abortion
property_value: Property:P5191 GSSO:004413
property_value: wiki:Q1823134 "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2012004097" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: GSSO:009974
name: sex-selective abortion
def: "The practice of terminating a pregnancy based upon the predicted sex of the infant. The selective abortion of female fetuses is most common where male children are valued over female children, especially in parts of East Asia and South Asia (particularly in countries such as People's Republic of China, India and Pakistan), as well as in the Caucasus, Western Balkans, and to a lesser extent North America." []
is_a: GSSO:009975 ! selective abortion
property_value: Property:P5191 GSSO:004413
property_value: schema:alternateName "sex-selective abortions" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:009975
name: selective abortion
def: "Abortion in which a characteristic or characteristics of the fetus or the pregnancy is not preferred for any reason (including if the abortion is therapeutic to the pregnant person)." []
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q91945103
is_a: GSSO:004414 ! induced abortion
property_value: Property:P3201 "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MEDDRA/10067499" xsd:anyURI
property_value: Property:P5191 GSSO:004413
property_value: schema:alternateName "selective abortions" xsd:string

