[Term]
id: GSSO:009977
name: birth control sabotage
def: "A form of reproductive coercion which involves tampering with contraception or interfering with the use of contraception. Birth control sabotage includes removing a condom after agreeing to wear one (also called stealthing), damaging a condom, removing contraception (including vaginal rings, intrauterine devices (IUDs), and contraceptive patches), or throwing away oral contraceptive pills. Other methods of birth control sabotage include preventing a partner from obtaining or refilling contraceptive prescriptions, refusing to wear a condom, stating that a condom is being worn when one is not, not withdrawing after agreeing to do so, exaggerating the risks of hormonal contraceptives, and not telling a partner if a condom broke or fell off." []
synonym: "birth-control sabotage" EXACT []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reproductive_coercion#Birth_control_sabotage
is_a: GSSO:009971 ! reproductive coercion

[Term]
id: GSSO:009978
name: controlling the outcome of a pregnancy
def: "An attempt to influence a partner to continue or terminate a pregnancy. This can include abortion coercion, or pressuring, threatening, or forcing a partner to have an abortion or not." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reproductive_coercion#Controlling_the_outcome_of_a_pregnancy
is_a: GSSO:009971 ! reproductive coercion

