[Term]
id: GSSO:010036
name: Modern Minoan paganism
def: "A form of paganism which purports to derive from ancient Minoan religion; because little is known of that religion, however, it is not considered reconstructionist, and therefore also oftentimes incorporates a ritual framework descended from Gardnerian Wicca." []
synonym: "Minoan tradition" RELATED [] {schema:alternateName="Minoan traditions"}
