property_value: wiki:Q1823134 "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85118706" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: GSSO:010044
name: Yoruba religion
def: "The traditional religious and spiritual concepts and practice of the Yoruba tribe. Its homeland is in present-day Southwestern Nigeria which comprised Oyo, Ogun, Osun, Ondo, Ekiti, and Kwara as well as Lagos States, parts of Kogi state and the adjoining parts of Benin and Togo, commonly known as Yorubaland. It shares some parallels with the Vodun practiced by the neighboring Fon and Ewe peoples to the west and to the religion of the Edo people to the east." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Yoruba_religion
