[Term]
id: GSSO:010323
name: anti-gender movement
def: "A social movement which opposes what is referred to as \"gender ideology\", a term which does not have a coherent definition. Individuals belonging to the movement typically oppose the distinction between sex and gender, oppose the ability for transgender persons (especially children) to access appropriate medical care, oppose discussion of gender theory and studies in schools, and oftentimes hold other relatively conservative views, such as opposing same-sex marriage. The movement derives from Catholic theology beginning in the 1990s, but the protests which brought the movement to attention did not start until around 2012–2013." []
synonym: "anti-gender countermovement" RELATED []
