[Term]
id: GSSO:010511
name: lesbian-trans turf wars transition cohort
def: "An American transition cohort defined by Avery Everhart as beginning with the rise of the so-called \"lesbian-trans turf wars\", which succeeded the \"Butch/FTM Border Wars\" of the late 1990s. Everhart does not give beginning and/or end dates to this cohort, but notes that it was contemporaneous with the \"early Tumblr\" transition cohort, which probably lasted from about 2007 up until 2013." []
is_a: GSSO:010507 ! American gender transition cohort
property_value: seeAlso GSSO:011976

[Term]
id: GSSO:010512
name: early Tumblr transition cohort
def: "An American transition cohort defined by Avery Everhart as beginning with the rise of the social networking website Tumblr. Although Everhart does not specify the timeframe, Tumblr was founded in 2007 and Yahoo! Inc. acquired Tumblr in 2013, which could be considered as \"bookending\" the \"early Tumblr\" era." []
is_a: GSSO:010507 ! American gender transition cohort

[Term]
id: GSSO:010513
name: TS Roadmap transition cohort
def: "An American transition cohort defined by Avery Everhart as beginning with New Year's Day 2000 (\"Y2K\" era) up to 2009. The cohort is named after the popular website \"TS Roadmap\" (now known as \"Transgender Roadmap\") created by Andrea James." []
