[Term]
id: GSSO:010536
name: modern society
def: "The ensemble of particular socio-cultural norms, attitudes and practices that arose in the wake of the Renaissance—in the \"Age of Reason\" of 17th-century thought and the 18th-century \"Enlightenment\"." []
comment: Depending on the field, "modernity" may refer to different time periods or qualities. In historiography, the 17th and 18th centuries are usually described as early modern, while the long 19th century corresponds to "modern history" proper. While it includes a wide range of interrelated historical processes and cultural phenomena (from fashion to modern warfare), it can also refer to the subjective or existential experience of the conditions they produce, and their ongoing impact on human culture, institutions, and politics.
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Modernity
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modernity
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q11084414
is_a: GSSO:010535 ! society
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "modernity" xsd:string
property_value: schema:alternateName "modern societies" xsd:string

