[Term]
id: GSSO:010548
name: technocritical theory
def: "A branch of critical theory devoted to the study of technological change. Technocriticism treats technological transformation as historically specific changes in personal and social practices of research, invention, regulation, distribution, promotion, appropriation, use, and discourse, rather than as an autonomous or socially indifferent accumulation of useful inventions, or as an uncritical narrative of linear \"progress\", \"development\" or \"innovation\"." []
