id: GSSO:010550
name: algorithmic bias
def: "Any of various systematic and repeatable errors in a computer system that create unfair outcomes, such as privileging one arbitrary group of users over others. Bias can emerge due to many factors, including but not limited to the design of the algorithm or the unintended or unanticipated use or decisions relating to the way data is coded, collected, selected or used to train the algorithm. Algorithmic bias is found across platforms, including but not limited to search engine results and social media platforms, and can have impacts ranging from inadvertent privacy violations to reinforcing social biases of race, gender, sexuality, and ethnicity." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algorithmic_bias
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q45253460
is_a: GSSO:006773 ! statistical bias
property_value: schema:alternateName "algorithmic biases" xsd:string

