[Term]
id: GSSO:010570
name: Weird Twitter subculture
def: "A loose subculture of internet humor dedicated to publication of humorous material on Twitter that is disorganized and hard to explain. Related to anti-humor and created primarily by Twitter users who are not professional humorists, Weird Twitter-style jokes may be presented as disorganized thoughts, rather than in a conventional joke format or punctuated sentence structure. Related accounts include originators such as dril and, more tangentially, authors such as poet Patricia Lockwood." []
synonym: "\"Weird Twitter\" subculture" EXACT []
