[Term]
id: GSSO:010571
name: anthroposphere
def: "The part of the environment that is made or modified by humans for use in human activities and human habitats. The anthroposphere can be viewed as a human-generated equivalent to the biosphere. While the biosphere is the total biomass of the Earth and its interaction with its systems, the anthroposphere is the total mass of human-generated systems and materials, including the human population, and its interaction with the Earth's systems. However, while the biosphere is able to efficiently produce and recycle materials through processes like photosynthesis and decomposition, the anthroposphere is highly inefficient at sustaining itself." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthroposphere
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q574518
is_a: ENVO:01001784 ! compound astronomical body part

[Term]
id: GSSO:010572
name: technosphere
def: "The part of the physical environment that is made up of technological objects manufactured by humans." []
is_a: GSSO:010571 ! anthroposphere

[Term]
id: GSSO:010573
name: logosphere
def: "Originally referred to the metaphysical space made of up possible interpretations of words' meanings based on language and context. Today, the term \"logosphere\" is often used to refer to \"the sum-total of ideas, concepts and facts that inhabit the collective texts — digital, printed, handwritten, carved or otherwise — of the human race\", therefore the logosphere is a subspace of the infosphere." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logosphere
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q6667858
is_a: GSSO:010566 ! infosphere

