[Term]
id: GSSO:010577
name: copycat law
def: "A law (or bill) which originates from a non-legislative organization,  which is then sent to multiple legislatures, often with little to no change in language. Such laws often originate from corporations or non-governmental organizations (NGOs) which push particular agendas (such is the case with anti-abortion groups, far-right groups, etc.)." []
