[Term]
id: GSSO:010667
name: thyroplasty
def: "A phonosurgical technique designed to improve the voice by altering the thyroid cartilage of the larynx (the voice box), which houses the vocal cords in order to change the position or the length of the vocal cords." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thyroplasty
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q28455267
is_a: GSSO:010666 ! thyroid cartilage reconstruction
property_value: Property:P3201 "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MEDDRA/10074455" xsd:anyURI
property_value: Property:P5806 "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/SNOMEDCT/820511000168109" xsd:anyURI
property_value: schema:alternateName "thyroplasties" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:010668
name: type 1 thyroplasty
def: "A type of thyroplasty in which a rectangular portion of the thyroid cartilage is mobilized and pushed towards the medial side using a piece of silastic block of proper shape under local anesthesia." []
is_a: GSSO:010667 ! thyroplasty
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "medialization thyroplasty" xsd:string {schema:alternateName="medialization thyroplasties"}
property_value: schema:alternateName "type 1 thyroplasties" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:010669
name: type 2 thyroplasty
def: "A surgical procedure used in conditions like adductor spasmodic dysphonia (a condition in which there is distortion of the voice due to excessively tight closure of the glottis on phonation). Generally, lateralization thyroplasty is intended to prevent this tight closure of the glottis at the terminal stage of phonation by lateralizing the position of the vocal cord. During this procedure, an incision is made at midline of the thyroid cartilage. A silicon wedge is used to fix the incised thyroid cartilage in the newly abducted position." []
is_a: GSSO:010667 ! thyroplasty
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "lateralization thyroplasty" xsd:string {schema:alternateName="lateralization thyroplasties"}
property_value: schema:alternateName "type 2 thyroplasties" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:010670
name: type 3 thyroplasty
def: "A procedure performed in order to lower the vocal pitch by shortening the thyroid ala. It is performed by antero-posterior shortening of the thyroid ala." []
is_a: GSSO:010667 ! thyroplasty
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "relaxation thyroplasty" xsd:string {schema:alternateName="relaxation thyroplasties"}
property_value: schema:alternateName "type 2 thyroplasties" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:010671
name: type 4 thyroplasty
def: "A type of thyroplasty performed to elevate vocal pitch. This procedure consists of lengthening of the thyroid cartilage. It includes cricothyroid approximation." []
synonym: "cricothyroid approximation" NARROW [] {Property:P1813="CTA", schema:alternateName="cricothyroid approximations"}
is_a: GSSO:010667 ! thyroplasty
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "stretching thyroplasty" xsd:string {schema:alternateName="stretching thyroplasties"}
property_value: schema:alternateName "type 4 thyroplasties" xsd:string

