[Term]
id: GSSO:010711
name: lip lift
def: "A plastic surgery procedure that modifies the appearance of the lips by reshaping them to increase the prominence of the vermilion border." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lip_lift
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q6556148
is_a: GSSO:010722 ! cheiloplasty
property_value: schema:alternateName "lip lifts" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:010712
name: direct lip lift
def: "A surgical technique for increasing the prominence (display) of the vermilion coloring of the lips, by removing skin (and other tissues) as required, ether directly from or from above the white line of skin that borders onto, and sets off, the vermilion of the lips (the white roll). The incisions remove tissue and significantly alter the shape of the lips by moving up the vermilion from both peaks of the Cupid's bow outwards to the commissures, the corners of the mouth. Incisions are also made below the lower lip to increase the projection of the vermilion of the lower lip." []
is_a: GSSO:010711 ! lip lift
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "gull-wing lift" xsd:string {schema:alternateName="gull-wing lifts"}
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "gullwing lip lift" xsd:string {schema:alternateName="gullwing lip lifts"}
property_value: Property:P1813 "DLL" xsd:string
property_value: schema:alternateName "direct lip lifts" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:010713
name: subnasal bullhorn lip lift
def: "A technical variant of the gull-wing lip lift is the sub-nasal lip lift (bull-horn lip lift), which involves the removal of either an ellipse or a curved-edge ellipse of tissue from under the nose. The skin then is raised, and sutured to lift the lip and expose more of the upper-lip vermilion. Depending upon the indications of the patient, this technique can increase the drooping the corners of the mouth (commissures); thus, the sub-nasal lip lift often includes a corner-lift surgical step. In the corner lift procedure (external angle oral commissuroplasty), triangles of tissue are resected from above the commissures, thereby elevating the corners of the mouth.[3] A descending wedge of tissue can also be removed to add contour to the Cupid's bow or to reduce bulky lips." []
is_a: GSSO:010723 ! indirect lip lift
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "subnasal bullhorn indirect lip lift" xsd:string {schema:alternateName="subnasal bullhorn indirect lip lifts", Property:P1813="subnasal bullhorn ILL"}
property_value: schema:alternateName "subnasal bullhorn lip lifts" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:010714
name: central lip lift
def: "A lip lift technique similar to the subnasal bullhorn lift, which involves shortening the space between the lips and the nose by using an incision at the lower nose." []
is_a: GSSO:010723 ! indirect lip lift
property_value: schema:alternateName "central lip lifts" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:010715
name: corner lip lift
def: "A lip lift procedure which consists of a lenticular excision of the white skin surrounding the upper oral commissure in order to lift this part of the lips." []
synonym: "lip corner lift" EXACT [] {schema:alternateName="lip corner lifts"}
is_a: GSSO:010711 ! lip lift
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "corner of the mouth lift" xsd:string {schema:alternateName="corner of the mouth lifts", Property:P1813="CML"}
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "grin lift" xsd:string {schema:alternateName="grin lifts"}
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "smile lift" xsd:string {schema:alternateName="smile lifts"}
property_value: schema:alternateName "corner lip lifts" xsd:string

