[Term]
id: GSSO:010994
name: appeal to consequences
def: "An informal fallacy that concludes a hypothesis (typically a belief) to be either true or false based on whether the premise leads to desirable or undesirable consequences. It is a fallacy because the desirability of a premise's consequence does not make the premise true." []
