property_value: schema:alternateName "patrifocal families" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:011003
name: avuncular family
def: "A family unit consisting of at least one grandparent, parent, parent's sibling, and child." []
is_a: GSSO:003265 ! familie
property_value: schema:alternateName "avuncular families" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:011004
name: extended family
def: "A family unit in which parents and their children co-reside with other members of one parent's family." []
is_a: GSSO:003265 ! familie
property_value: Property:P1036 "306.857" xsd:decimal {schema:bookEdition="20"}
property_value: schema:alternateName "extended families" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:011005
name: immediate family
def: "A defined group of relations, used in rules or laws to determine which members of a person's family are affected by those rules. It normally includes a person's parents, siblings, spouses, children, or an individual related genetically whose close association is an equivalent of a family relationship. It can contain others connected by birth, adoption, marriage, civil partnership, or cohabitation, such as grandparents, great-grandparents, grandchildren, great-grandchildren, aunts, uncles, siblings-in-law, half-siblings, cousins, adopted children and step-parents/step-children, and cohabiting partners." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immediate_family
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q6004774
is_a: GSSO:003265 ! familie

[Term]
id: GSSO:011006
name: evolutionary psychology
def: "A theoretical approach which purports to examine psychological structure from an evolutionary perspective. Evolutionary psychologists hold that behaviors or traits that occur universally in all cultures are good candidates for evolutionary adaptations." []
comment: In many cases, "evolutionary psychology" has become a dogwhistle for ethnocentrism, white nationalism, and eugenics. Evolutionary psychologists have claimed that rape is an evolutionary adaptation, that the "hourglass" figure in women is a result of evolution, that phobias are innate, that being gay is a "maladaptive" behavior, and that IQ and race are linked at a genetic level (a form of scientific racism).\n\nMultiple evolutionary psychologists, including Marc Hauser and Diederik Stapel have admitted to fabricating evidence to support their theories.\n\nThe field as a whole should be suspect, as should individuals claiming the label of evolutionary psychology.
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Evolutionary_psychology
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evolutionary_psychology
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q219695
is_a: GSSO:006201 ! psychology
property_value: terms:isReferencedBy books?id=5qHGELC:h-4C
property_value: terms:isReferencedBy https://doi.org/10.1177/0022167819899009

[Term]
id: GSSO:011008
name: anarcho-capitalism
def: "A fringe political philosophy and economic theory that advocates the elimination of centralized states in favor of a system of private property enforced by private agencies, free markets and the right-libertarian interpretation of self-ownership, which extends the concept to include control of private property as part of the self." []
comment: Despite the name, anarcho-capitalism is not a form of anarchism. Its labeling as such attempts to appeal to particular groups of individuals; it is mainly furthered by American reactionary think tanks.
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anarcho-capitalism
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q192424
is_a: GSSO:003817 ! capitalism

[Term]
id: GSSO:011009
name: LGBTQ assimilation
def: "A process in which LGBTQIA+ persons or groups desire to resemble dominant, cisheteronormative society or assume the values, behaviors, and beliefs of that society." []
synonym: "LGBT assimilation" NARROW []
synonym: "queer assimilation" RELATED []
is_a: GSSO:003105 ! cultural assimilation
property_value: Property:P5191 GSSO:000586

[Term]
id: GSSO:011010
name: homonormative assimilation
def: "A process in which gay persons or groups desire to resemble dominant, heteronormative society or assume the values, behaviors, and beliefs of that society." []
comment: Homonormative assimilation typically implies that gay people who fit cultural expectations in heteronormative society should be allowed to exist, and is often connected to ideas like effeminophobia.
is_a: GSSO:011009 ! LGBTQ assimilation

[Term]
id: GSSO:011011
name: transnormative assimilation
def: "A process in which trans persons or groups desire to resemble dominant, cisnormative society or assume the values, behaviors, and beliefs of that society." []
comment: Transnormative assimilation is often connected to "trutrans" ideologies and transmedicalism; these ways of thinking often imply that only cisgender passing binary trans persons should be allowed to exist.
is_a: GSSO:011009 ! LGBTQ assimilation

[Term]
id: GSSO:011015
name: Amazon feminism
def: "A third-wave feminism which has been used with two slightly different meanings: (1) a feminism in which women should think of themselves as warriors in every moment, behaving as equals to men; and (2) a feminism which emphasizes female physical prowess as a means to achieving gender equality." []
is_a: GSSO:003859 ! third-wave feminism
property_value: Property:P5191 GSSO:002229

[Term]
id: GSSO:011016
