[Term]
id: GSSO:011017
name: germ theory denialism
def: "The false belief that microscopic organisms such as bacteria and viruses do not cause disease, despite a number of validations of the work of many scientists in showcasing that such organisms are indeed the causative agents of infectious diseases." []
