[Term]
id: GSSO:011076
name: metropolitan area
def: "A region consisting of a densely populated urban core and its less-populated surrounding territories under the same administrative jurisdiction, sharing industries, commercial areas, transport network, infrastructures and housing. A metro area usually comprises multiple jurisdictions and municipalities: neighborhoods, townships, boroughs, cities, towns, exurbs, suburbs, counties, districts, and even states and nations like the eurodistricts. As social, economic and political institutions have changed, metropolitan areas have become key economic and political regions." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Metropolitan_areas
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metropolitan_area
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1907114
is_a: ENVO:00000004 ! administrative region
