[Term]
id: GSSO:011079
name: exurban area
def: "An area outside the typically denser inner suburban area of a metropolitan area, which has an economic and commuting connection to the metro area, low housing density, and growth. It shapes an interface between urban and rural landscapes holding an urban nature for its functional, economic, and social interaction with the urban center, due to its dominant residential character." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exurb
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q65122088
is_a: ENVO:00000004 ! administrative region
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "exurb" xsd:string
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "exurbs" xsd:string
property_value: schema:alternateName "exurban areas" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:011080
name: urban area
def: "A human settlement with a high population density and infrastructure of built environment. Urban areas are created through urbanization and are categorized by urban morphology as cities, towns, conurbations or suburbs. In urbanism, the term contrasts to rural areas such as villages and hamlets; in urban sociology or urban anthropology it contrasts with natural environment." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Urban_areas
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urban_area
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q702492
is_a: GSSO:011076 ! metropolitan area
property_value: schema:alternateName "urban areas" xsd:string

