[Term]
id: GSSO:011105
name: identity-first language
def: "A type of linguistic prescription which intends to prioritize identity, usually by having an aspect of one's identity come before a general term (such as person, man, or woman). For instance, using \"autistic person\" rather than \"person with autism\"." []
synonym: "identity first language" EXACT []
is_a: http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D007802 ! language

[Term]
id: GSSO:011106
name: person-centered language
def: "A type of linguistic prescription, instead of being a replacement linguistic rule, promotes prioritizing the preferences of those who are being referred to and argues for greater nuance in the language used to describe people and groups of people. Usually placed in contrast to people-first language and identity-first language." []
is_a: http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D007802 ! language
property_value: Property:P5191 SIO:000498

