[Term]
id: GSSO:011110
name: Chicanismo
def: "The ideology cited as underpinning the Chicano movement, focusing on a strong sense of self-identity and cultural affiration achieved by solidifying a new sense of Mexican-American nationalism, drawing ties to the long-forgotten history of Chicanos in lands that were very recently Mexican, and creating a symbolic connection to the ancestral ties of Mesoamerica and the Nahuatl language." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicanismo
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5095930
is_a: GSSO:002945 ! ethnicity-related social ideology

[Term]
id: GSSO:011111
name: Xicanisma
def: "An ideology which emerged as a recognition of the shift in consciousness since the Chicano Movement, starting in the 1990s and early 2000s, which aimed to reassert the need to form coalitions with other oppressed ethnic groups as strategic alliances." []
is_a: GSSO:002945 ! ethnicity-related social ideology
