[Term]
id: GSSO:011283
name: deviationism
def: "A political ideology which expresses deviation which does not accord with a mainstream doctrine for a given time and/or area." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deviationism
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2789476
is_a: GSSO:002225 ! political ideology
is_a: GSSO:002938 ! social ideology

[Term]
id: GSSO:011284
name: revisionism
def: "A deviationist political ideology which is based upon significant revision of fundamental premises of a given time and/or place, especially those which ideologies which are irrational in nature." []
synonym: "revisionist" RELATED []
is_a: GSSO:011283 ! deviationism

[Term]
id: GSSO:011285
name: denialism
def: "A form of deviationism which imploys denial of fundamental premises, often irrationally." []
synonym: "denialist" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Denialism
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denialism
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q10567262
is_a: GSSO:011283 ! deviationism
property_value: seeAlso GSSO:005269
property_value: wiki:Q1823134 "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2017004461" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: GSSO:011286
name: dogmatism
def: "A form of deviationist ideology predicated on beliefs held with unquestionable certainty, often without critical interrogation of those beliefs." []
synonym: "dogmatic" RELATED []
synonym: "dogmatist" RELATED []
is_a: GSSO:011283 ! deviationism

[Term]
id: GSSO:011287
name: ivermectinism
def: "A particular subtype of COVID-19 denialism focused on denial of the effectiveness of COVID-19 vaccines, followed by claims that other, unproven and unscientific folk remedies (such as essential oils, bleach, hydroxychloroquine, ivermectin) can effect the course of COVID-19 in any discernible way." []
is_a: GSSO:010622 ! COVID-19 denialism

[Term]
id: GSSO:011288
name: vaccine denialism
def: "The false belief that vaccines do not work, or that some aspect of the vaccines has been exaggerated or fabricated by the medical community or world governments, such as the claim that vaccines cause autism or gender dysphoria, among other things." []
is_a: GSSO:010621 ! medical denialism

