name: normativism
def: "An ideology which advocates in regard to the primacy of or the desirability of social norms, or the current socio-political norm; contrast with deviationism." []
synonym: "normativ" RELATED [https://lgbt.dk/ordbog/normativ/]
synonym: "normative" RELATED []
synonym: "normativist" RELATED []
synonym: "normativity" RELATED []
is_a: GSSO:002225 ! political ideology
is_a: GSSO:002938 ! social ideology

[Term]
id: GSSO:011302
name: aetonormativity
def: "Any assumption of an age-based norm and particularly the assumption that adults and adult experiences are normative while children and childish experiences are consequently deviant or other." []
synonym: "adult normative" RELATED []
synonym: "aetonormative" RELATED []
is_a: GSSO:011305 ! age normativity
property_value: oboInOwl:hasSynonym "adult normativity" xsd:string
property_value: Property:P3938 http://isni.org/isni/0000000114472955 {dc:date="2009"}

[Term]
id: GSSO:011303
name: metronormativity
def: "The ideology that metropolitan or urban areas and populations are prioritized over other areas, such as those that are rural or suburban." []
synonym: "metronormative" RELATED []
is_a: GSSO:011306 ! environmental normativity

[Term]
id: GSSO:011304
name: queer metronormativity
def: "Normativity in LGBTQIA+ communities in which the metropolitan is prioritized as a mode of acceptance, i.e. the only way of achieving happiness and open existence." []
synonym: "queer metronormative" RELATED []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queer_anti-urbanism#Queer_metronormativity
is_a: GSSO:011303 ! metronormativity
property_value: Property:P5191 GSSO:012413

