[Term]
id: GSSO:011461
name: lesbian ball
def: "Any of various lesbian events involving ballroom dancing." []
comment: Magnus Hirschfeld mentioned such balls in his book Berlins drittes Geschlect (1904): "In a big hall, where the uranians celebrate their balls, every week there is an equivalent evening ball for uranierinnen, most of whom participate in men's clothing. Most homosexual women can be found at the same spot every year on the costume ball a lady from Berlin organizes. The ball is not public, but usually only accessible those that are known to one of the ladies on the committee."
