[Term]
id: GSSO:011741
name: fatigue syndrome
def: "An informal grouping of syndromes in which the major symptom is fatigue." []
comment: Note that, fatigue syndromes are classed as psychiatric syndromes based on fatigue being described as a psychiatric symptom because it is a relatively subjective experience. However, fatigue (and fatigue syndromes) can be caused by somatic conditions, such as infections, malignancies, autoimmune disorders, anxiety, and depression, among other things.
is_a: GSSO:000517 ! psychiatric syndrome
property_value: schema:alternateName "fatigue syndromes" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:011742
name: chronic fatigue syndrome
def: "A clinical diagnosis characterized by an unexplained persistent or relapsing chronic fatigue that is of at least six months' duration, is not the result of ongoing exertion, is not substantially alleviated by rest, and results in substantial reduction of previous levels of occupational, educational, social, or personal activities. Common concurrent symptoms of at least six months duration include impairment of memory or concentration, diffuse pain, sore throat, tender lymph nodes, headaches of a new type, pattern, or severity, and nonrestorative sleep." []
synonym: "GSSO:011746" RELATED []
synonym: "myalgic encephalomyelitis/chronic fatigue syndrome" BROAD [] {Property:P1813="ME/CFS"}
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Chronic_fatigue_syndrome
