[Term]
id: GSSO:011769
name: sovereign citizen movement
def: "A loose grouping of primarily American litigants, commentators, tax protesters, and financial-scheme promoters, who claim to be answerable only to their particular interpretations of the common law and to not be subject to any government statutes or proceedings. In the United States, they do not recognize U.S. currency and maintain that they are \"free of any legal constraints\". They especially reject most forms of taxation as illegitimate. Participants in the movement argue this concept in opposition to the idea of \"federal citizens\", who, they say, have unknowingly forfeited their rights by accepting some aspect of federal law." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Sovereign_citizen_movement
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sovereign_citizen_movement
