[Term]
id: GSSO:012094
name: bathroom legislation
def: "Legislation that defines access to public toilets by gender (restrooms)—or for  transgender individuals. Bathroom bills affect access to sex-segregated public facilities for an individual based on a determination of their sex as defined in some specific way—such as their sex as assigned at birth, their sex as listed on their birth certificate, or the sex that corresponds to their gender identity." []
is_a: GSSO:012093 ! anti-transgender legislation

[Term]
id: GSSO:012095
name: adultery law
def: "Any of various laws relating to extramarital sex. Historically, many cultures considered adultery a very serious crime, some subject to severe punishment, especially in the case of extramarital sex involving a married woman and a man other than her husband, with penalties including capital punishment, mutilation, or torture. Such punishments have gradually fallen into disfavor, especially in Anglosphere and European countries from the 19th century. In countries where adultery is still a criminal offense, punishments range from fines to caning and even capital punishment. Since the 20th century, criminal laws against adultery have become controversial, with most countries repealing them." []
comment: Most countries that criminalize adultery are those where the dominant religion is Islam, and several Sub-Saharan African Christian-majority countries, but there are some notable exceptions to this rule, namely Philippines and 17 U.S. states.
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adultery_laws
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107630986
is_a: GSSO:003146 ! family law
is_a: GSSO:003167 ! sex law
property_value: schema:alternateName "adultery laws" xsd:string

[Term]
id: GSSO:012096
name: bed
def: "A piece of furniture which is used as a place to sleep, rest, and relax. Most modern beds consist of a soft, cushioned mattress on a bed frame. The mattress rests either on a solid base, often wood slats, or a sprung base. Many beds include a box spring inner-sprung base, which is a large mattress-sized box containing wood and springs that provide additional support and suspension for the mattress." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bed
