[Term]
id: GSSO:012166
name: Brotherhood of the Golden Arrow
name: Confrerie de la Flèche d'Or
def: "Occult society formed by Russian occultist and mystic Maria de Naglowska in Paris in 1932. Naglowska's occult teaching centered on what she called the Third Term of the Trinity, in which the Holy Spirit of the classic Christian trinity is recognized as the divine feminine. Her practices aimed to bring about a reconciliation of the light and dark forces in nature through the union of the masculine and feminine, revealing the spiritually transformative power of sex." []
is_a: GSSO:012151 ! Rosicrucianism

[Term]
id: GSSO:012168
name: Dianism
def: "A 19th-century American spiritual sexual practice consisting of \"sexual satisfaction from sexual contact\" but without ejaculation. The practice was named for Diana, the Roman goddess of chastity, by American court reporter and astronomer Henry M. Parkhurst in his 1882 pamphlet Diana. In the 1890s, sexual mystic Ida Craddock included Dianism as part of her teachings. In the 20th century, the practice found favor with American followers of Aleister Crowley, most notably C.F. Russell." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dianism
