[Term]
id: GSSO:012576
name: Ukrainian Soviet Socialist Republic
def: "The original name of Soviet Ukraine in 1919 was Ukrainian Socialist Soviet Republic, but after the ratification of the 1936 Soviet Constitution, the names of all Soviet republics were changed, transposing the second (socialist) and third (soviet or radianska in Ukrainian) words. In accordance, on 5 December 1936, the 8th Extraordinary Congress Soviets in Soviet Union changed the name of the republic to the Ukrainian Soviet Socialist Republic, which was ratified by the 14th Extraordinary Congress of Soviets in Ukrainian SSR on 31 January 1937." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Ukrainian_Soviet_Socialist_Republic
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukrainian_Soviet_Socialist_Republic
