[Term]
id: GSSO:012675
name: in vitro fertilization with intracytoplasmic sperm injection
def: "An in vitro fertilization (IVF) procedure in which a single sperm cell is injected directly into the cytoplasm of an egg. This technique is used in order to prepare the gametes for the obtention of embryos that may be transferred to a maternal uterus. With this method, the acrosome reaction is skipped." []
