[Term]
id: GSSO:012755
name: Hindu philosophy
def: "Any of the various philosophies, world views and teachings of Hinduism that emerged in Ancient India. These include six systems (shad-darśana) – Sankhya, Yoga, Nyaya, Vaisheshika, Mimamsa and Vedanta." []
