[Term]
id: GSSO:012902
name: bisexual theory
def: "A field of critical theory, inspired by queer theory and bisexual politics, that foregrounds bisexuality as both a theoretical focus and as an epistemology. Bisexual theory emerged most prominently in the 1990s, in response to the burgeoning queer studies movement, employing a similar post-structuralist approach but redressing queer theory’s tendency towards bisexual erasure." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bisexual_theory
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q65047280
is_a: GSSO:002356 ! critical theory
property_value: seeAlso GSSO:002255
