[Term]
id: NCBITaxon:50557
name: insect
def: "A taxonomic class of arthropods that includes praying mantises, dragonflies, grasshoppers, true bugs, flies, bees, wasps, ants, butterflies, moths, and beetles." []
def: "Members of the phylum Arthropoda composed or organisms characterized by division into three parts: head, thorax, and abdomen. They are the dominant group of animals on earth with several hundred thousand different kinds. Three orders, Hemiptera; Diptera; and Siphonaptera; are of medical interest in that they cause disease in humans and animals." []
