[Term]
id: NCBITaxon:7434
name: aculeate
def: "A subclade of Hymenoptera. The name is a reference to the defining feature of the group, which is the modification of the ovipositor into a stinger (thus, the group could be called \"stinging wasps\", though the group also contains the ants and the bees). In other words, the structure that was originally used to lay eggs is modified instead to deliver venom." []
