[Term]
id: NCIT:C120191
name: complete androgen insensitivity syndrome
def: "A condition that results in the complete inability of the cell to respond to androgens. As such, the insensitivity to androgens is only clinically significant when it occurs in genetic males (i.e. individuals with a Y chromosome, or more specifically, an SRY gene)." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Complete_androgen_insensitivity_syndrome
