[Term]
id: NCIT:C124436
name: sex at birth
def: "The assigned sex by any of various entities or institutions based (typically) on the observable, physical sexual characteristics of the neonate at birth." []
comment: Avoid this term where possible and be more specific when absolutely necessary (typically only in some medical settings); when referring to sex use either "external organ-based sex" or "gonadal sex" (for instance, when a sex for clinical use is necessary); when referring to gender (such as a legal or administrative designation) use "assigned gender at birth".
