[Term]
id: UBERON:0002365
name: exocrine gland
def: "A gland from which secretions reach a free surface of the body by ducts." []
def: "A gland that secretes products (excluding hormones and other chemical messengers) into ducts (duct glands) which lead directly into the external environment. Typical exocrine glands include sweat glands, salivary glands, mammary glands, stomach, liver, pancreas." []
