[Term]
id: UBERON:0010516
name: clasper
def: "A male anatomical structure found some groups of animals, used in mating. Male cartilaginous fish have claspers formed from the posterior portion of their pelvic fin which serve as intromittent organs used to channel semen into the female's cloaca during mating. The act of mating in some fish including sharks usually includes one of the claspers raised to allow water into the siphon through a specific orifice. The clasper is then inserted into the vagina, where it opens like an umbrella to anchor its position. The siphon then begins to contract expelling water and sperm. Male chimaeras have cephalic claspers on their heads, which are thought to aid in holding the female during mating." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clasper
xref: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q35413
is_a: UBERON:0008811 ! intromittent organ
property_value: Property:P1554 "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0010516" xsd:anyURI
property_value: schema:alternateName "claspers" xsd:string
property_value: wiki:Q1823134 "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh93009355" xsd:anyURI

[Term]
id: UBERON:0010517
name: cephalic clasper
def: "A mace-like spiny-headed rod found on the mid-dorsal surface of heads of male Holocephali. Thought to aid in holding the female during copulation." []
is_a: UBERON:0010516 ! clasper
property_value: Property:P1554 "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0010517" xsd:anyURI
property_value: schema:alternateName "cephalic claspers" xsd:string

[Term]
id: UBERON:0010518
name: pelvic fin clasper
def: "The rod-like extension of the medial portion of the pelvic fin in male Elasmobranchii and Holocephali. Claspers are used as intromittent organs (not in clasping), the grooves on their facing surfaces together forming a tube for the transmission of sperm when the claspers are held together. The anterior proximal opening is called the apopyle, the posterior distal opening the rhipidion." []
is_a: UBERON:0010516 ! clasper
property_value: Property:P1554 "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0010518" xsd:anyURI
property_value: schema:alternateName "pelvic fin claspers" xsd:string

