[Term]
id: http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D003577
name: cytochrome P450 dependent monooxygenase
def: "A superfamily of hundreds of closely related hemeproteins found throughout the phylogenetic spectrum, from animals, plants, fungi, to bacteria. They include numerous complex monooxygenases (mixed function oxygenases). In animals, these P-450 enzymes serve two major functions: (1) biosynthesis of steroids, fatty acids, and bile acids; (2) metabolism of endogenous and a wide variety of exogenous substrates, such as toxins and drugs (biotransformation). They are classified, according to their sequence similarities rather than functions, into CYP gene families (>40% homology) and subfamilies (>59% homology). For example, enzymes from the CYP1, CYP2, and CYP3 gene families are responsible for most drug metabolism." []
is_a: http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D006899 ! mixed function oxygenase
property_value: Property:P486 "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D003577" xsd:anyURI
property_value: schema:alternateName "cytochrome P450 dependent monooxygenases" xsd:string

