[Term]
id: http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D005783
name: cinsiyet kimliği {terms:isReferencedBy="https://web.archive.org/web/20190123175918/https://oramrefugee.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/Glossary-PDF.pdf"}
name: gender identity
name: identidad de género {terms:isReferencedBy="https://web.archive.org/web/20200102232435/lgbthealtheducation.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/National-LGBT-Health-Education-Center-Glossary.SPANISH-2018.pdf"}
name: identité de genre {terms:isReferencedBy="GSSO:011927", terms:isReferencedBy="https://web.archive.org/web/20190123175918/https://oramrefugee.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/04/Glossary-PDF.pdf"}
name: kønsidentitet {xref="https://lgbt.dk/ordbog/koensidentitet-2/"}
def: "A person's concept of self as being male and masculine or female and feminine, or ambivalent, based in part on physical characteristics, parental responses, and psychological and social pressures. It is the internal experience of gender role." []
def: "A person's sense of self as a member of a particular gender." []
comment: Note that while current models of gender support the idea that children categorize their own gender by around 3-6 years of age, personal conceptualization of gender identity can shift throughout a person's life (even within an individual category). Persons may identify with one, many, or no gender categories; additionally, pronoun use is not necessarily connected to gender identity.
synonym: "gender identity datum" RELATED [] {dc:identifier="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMRSE_00000133", schema:alternateName="gender identity data"}
synonym: "gender identity finding" RELATED [] {schema:alternateName="genderr identity findings", Property:P5806="http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/SNOMEDCT/285116001"}
synonym: "gender identity information content entity" RELATED [] {comment="This represents an information entity which is identification as a certain gender in some context. This datum may not represent a person's actual gender identity. For instance, if an individual has an online persona in which they identify as another gender, or if they lie (for instance, it may be safer for a pre-transition transgender person to lie about their gender identity in some contexts).", dc:identifier="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMRSE_00000209", schema:alternateName="gender identity information content entities"}
synonym: "self-identified gender identity" NARROW [] {comment="A person may self-identify as something other than their true gender identity for any of various reasons; therefore, sometimes it is more accurate to include \"self-identified gender identity\" rather than \"gender identity\", but in practice these values may be essentially synonymous.", schema:alternateName="self-identified gender identities", Property:P1813="SIGI"}
xref: https://data.nonbinary.wiki/wiki/Item\:Q7
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category\:Gender_identity
