[Term]
id: http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D005817
name: genetic counseling
def: "An educational process that provides information and advice to individuals or families about a genetic condition that may affect them. The purpose is to help individuals make informed decisions about marriage, reproduction, and other health management issues based on information about the genetic disease, the available diagnostic tests, and management programs. Psychosocial support is usually offered." []
