[Term]
id: http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma18307
name: infundibulum of uterine tube
def: "The second part of the uterine tube located between the purple ampulla and the fimbriae. The infundibulum terminates with the ostium of uterine tube, surrounded by fimbriae, one of which (the \"ovarian fimbria\") is attached to the ovary. Together, the infundibulum and fimbria find the oocyte after ovulation." []
