[Term]
id: http://purl.org/sig/ont/fma/fma18616
name: ovarian medulla
def: "Highly vascular stroma found in the center of the ovary that forms from embryonic mesenchyme and contains blood vessels, lymphatic vessels, and nerves; this stroma forms the tissue of the hilum by which the ovarian ligament is attached, and through which the blood vessels enter; it does not contain any ovarian follicles." []
def: "The central portion of the ovary, composed of loose connective tissue that contains blood vessels, lymph vessels and nerves." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medulla_of_ovary
